(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:09,950
(Space Rice Cake)

3
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:11,880
(The lunch rush was a huge success.)

4
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:13,450
(We made so much money!)

5
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:16,190
(Everything went smoothly thanks to Kyung Soo.)

6
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:19,120
(To hold on to Director Doh, )

7
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:21,760
(they quickly offered a new contract.)

8
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:24,760
(But in the dough-making match with his salary at stake, )

9
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:28,230
(Director Doh took an easy lead.)

10
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,270
(Meanwhile, our head chef...)

11
00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:32,670
(faced a crushing defeat.)

12
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:35,840
(And just like that, Director Doh took full control of the kitchen.)

13
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,610
(Give me an answer.)

14
00:00:38,110 --> 00:00:40,410
(He really whipped the kitchen into shape.)

15
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:44,120
(He was completely in his element at the stove.)

16
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:47,020
(Scanning the kitchen with his big eyes)

17
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:50,290
(His clear orders brought perfect order to the kitchen.)

18
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:53,830
(Thanks to him, the kitchen was running more smoothly.)

19
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:57,030
(But that peace didn't last long.)

20
00:00:57,030 --> 00:00:59,630
The meat inside the burger is undercooked.

21
00:00:59,930 --> 00:01:02,000
- The meat is undercooked?
- Yes.

22
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,200
- Young Ji, - Now, we're going to...

23
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,970
the customer said the burger patty was undercooked.

24
00:01:06,670 --> 00:01:08,110
- We enjoyed the food. Thank you.
- Thank you.

25
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:11,310
Is this supposed to be red here?

26
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:15,080
Would it be okay if I made you a fresh one?

27
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,150
Would that be okay? I ate some.

28
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,380
It's totally fine.

29
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:20,520
This is entirely our fault.

30
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:23,190
This has never happened before.

31
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:24,960
- I'll make you a fresh one.
- Okay.

32
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,690
- I'll make it right away.
- Thank you.

33
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:28,960
- Is this burger here okay?
- We shared it.

34
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:30,700
- Oh, you shared one burger?
- Yes.

35
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:32,760
- Do you need anything else?
- No, we're fine.

36
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:34,930
- My deepest apologies.
- That's okay.

37
00:01:35,170 --> 00:01:36,430
- I'll fix this for you right away.
- Okay.

38
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:38,670
I'll be back with your food as soon as possible.

39
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:41,710
- Is it cooked properly?
- It's slightly undercooked.

40
00:01:41,710 --> 00:01:43,640
- Oh, boy. But it's okay.
- I know how it happened.

41
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:46,880
I got confused and took a patty out after just four minutes.

42
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:48,110
- Four minutes?
- Yes.

43
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:51,250
(They were working on a new order.)

44
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:52,780
Serve them together.

45
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:54,290
Serve this with it.

46
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:55,590
Twenty.

47
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:56,890
- Nineteen.
- Nineteen.

48
00:01:57,190 --> 00:01:58,190
Eighteen.

49
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:00,560
- Let's go.
- Are we serving them together?

50
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:02,460
I'll make a perfect patty for them.

51
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:04,200
It's fine as long as we make it delicious.

52
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,200
A perfect patty for Table 11. I'm very sorry.

53
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,800
It's okay. You just have to be sure it tastes amazing. Don't worry.

54
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,000
I'm a disgrace to my family.

55
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:12,400
Did they order tacos as well?

56
00:02:12,670 --> 00:02:14,140
They seemed to be enjoying the tacos.

57
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:16,840
I was going to give them free tacos,

58
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:17,980
but they're already having tacos...

59
00:02:18,210 --> 00:02:19,310
How about a shrimp burger?

60
00:02:20,010 --> 00:02:21,280
Right. Let's give them a free shrimp burger.

61
00:02:21,610 --> 00:02:22,780
Let's give them a free shrimp burger.

62
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:26,580
(Barely holding it together, she starts by spreading the sauce.)

63
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,250
- Mi Hyun.
- Yes?

64
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:30,190
I fried this shrimp patty for five minutes. How does it look?

65
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:32,660
Give it a little longer. I'll take a look.

66
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:35,660
(Chef Mimi is also extra careful to make sure it's fully cooked.)

67
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:39,230
(She presses down on the patty like she's suppressing her sadness.)

68
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:41,400
Keep a watchful eye on the patty, Young Ji.

69
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:43,600
Just focus on the meat.

70
00:02:44,675 --> 00:02:46,175
I can do this.

71
00:02:47,415 --> 00:02:48,675
Young Ji can do it.

72
00:02:49,115 --> 00:02:50,985
Do you think it's still not fully cooked?

73
00:02:52,085 --> 00:02:53,345
It must be cooked to perfection.

74
00:02:55,315 --> 00:02:57,355
(Is it, really?)

75
00:02:57,785 --> 00:02:59,685
(She squirts water around the patty to create steam.)

76
00:02:59,985 --> 00:03:02,125
(Then she places a melting dome to cook it to the core.)

77
00:03:02,325 --> 00:03:03,525
Mimi, how does it look now?

78
00:03:04,495 --> 00:03:05,625
That's good. Perfect.

79
00:03:05,865 --> 00:03:07,595
(With the shrimp patty cleared, she checks the beef patty.)

80
00:03:07,595 --> 00:03:09,595
Okay. This must be fully cooked. I'm positive.

81
00:03:09,935 --> 00:03:11,705
I'll go and make things right.

82
00:03:12,005 --> 00:03:13,565
- Wait.
- Good luck.

83
00:03:14,505 --> 00:03:17,405
Such a terrible mistake will never happen again.

84
00:03:17,805 --> 00:03:19,245
Here's my secret weapon to make it up to you.

85
00:03:19,245 --> 00:03:21,445
- I brought a shrimp burger too.
- Oh, my.

86
00:03:21,445 --> 00:03:22,775
- You haven't tried it, have you?
- No.

87
00:03:23,145 --> 00:03:25,385
Such a thing cannot happen again.

88
00:03:25,585 --> 00:03:26,685
Thank you.

89
00:03:26,685 --> 00:03:28,215
- We'll enjoy...
- I am deeply sorry.

90
00:03:28,215 --> 00:03:30,385
- We'll enjoy it.
- Thank you. We'll enjoy it.

91
00:03:30,625 --> 00:03:31,625
(She leaves the table right away.)

92
00:03:31,685 --> 00:03:33,455
(Turning around)

93
00:03:35,325 --> 00:03:36,895
I'd like to see you take a bite before I go.

94
00:03:38,025 --> 00:03:39,095
Cut it in half.

95
00:03:39,095 --> 00:03:40,125
(They feel a bit of pressure.)

96
00:03:40,225 --> 00:03:42,395
- Our shrimp burger is really good.
- I see.

97
00:03:42,865 --> 00:03:45,065
The meat... I'm sure this one is fully cooked.

98
00:03:45,735 --> 00:03:47,575
Both of us work at a food company.

99
00:03:49,875 --> 00:03:50,905
I cooked it...

100
00:03:50,905 --> 00:03:52,545
- for 6 minutes and 30 seconds.
- I see.

101
00:03:52,905 --> 00:03:55,215
- I used a timer to cook it.
- Oh, I see.

102
00:03:55,215 --> 00:03:57,015
- Earlier, the meat was...
- How does it look?

103
00:03:57,015 --> 00:03:58,545
- It's cooked properly.
- Thank you.

104
00:03:58,545 --> 00:03:59,545
Please enjoy.

105
00:04:00,915 --> 00:04:02,855
And ma'am, we'll refund you for the beef burger.

106
00:04:02,855 --> 00:04:04,025
- I'm sorry again.
- But...

107
00:04:04,025 --> 00:04:05,525
- She said we'd get a refund.
- Oh, no, that's...

108
00:04:05,525 --> 00:04:06,755
(She runs away before they refuse.)

109
00:04:06,755 --> 00:04:07,755
Is it cooked properly?

110
00:04:07,755 --> 00:04:09,655
- Is it cooked properly?
- Yes. It's perfect.

111
00:04:10,825 --> 00:04:12,395
I saw them cut it open before I left.

112
00:04:13,395 --> 00:04:14,835
They work at a food company.

113
00:04:16,035 --> 00:04:17,235
- Really?
- Yes.

114
00:04:17,335 --> 00:04:18,405
We'll give Table 11...

115
00:04:18,405 --> 00:04:20,335
a refund for the beef burger.

116
00:04:20,335 --> 00:04:21,405
- Okay.
- I'm sorry.

117
00:04:21,605 --> 00:04:23,805
Don't be. It's okay.

118
00:04:24,105 --> 00:04:27,045
(During the burger incident, )

119
00:04:27,045 --> 00:04:29,115
(some of the customers finished their food and left.)

120
00:04:29,345 --> 00:04:31,615
(Thanks to the part-timer who works so fast, )

121
00:04:31,845 --> 00:04:34,815
(the tables are cleared immediately.)

122
00:04:34,985 --> 00:04:37,055
Now that we're moving more efficiently,

123
00:04:37,055 --> 00:04:38,855
have one less to serve,

124
00:04:39,285 --> 00:04:40,455
and Kyung Soo is working with us,

125
00:04:40,455 --> 00:04:41,925
- everything is running smoothly.
- Exactly.

126
00:04:41,925 --> 00:04:44,325
- Kyung Soo was the game changer.
- Right.

127
00:04:45,025 --> 00:04:48,465
Director Doh also came up with the tacos.

128
00:04:49,095 --> 00:04:51,635
(Right then, Director Doh, the all-rounder, returns.)

129
00:04:51,665 --> 00:04:52,835
Do you think...

130
00:04:53,265 --> 00:04:55,935
the part-timer will stick around to help prep for tomorrow?

131
00:04:56,135 --> 00:04:57,345
- What did you say?
- Pardon?

132
00:04:58,405 --> 00:05:01,515
I'm already done with my part here.

133
00:05:01,515 --> 00:05:02,675
Just until the end of the day.

134
00:05:03,345 --> 00:05:05,185
Then can you just help us with the dough?

135
00:05:06,215 --> 00:05:07,815
Doh Kyung Soo!

136
00:05:08,215 --> 00:05:09,615
- Doh Kyung Soo!
- Doh Kyung Soo!

137
00:05:09,615 --> 00:05:10,625
You must prep...

138
00:05:10,625 --> 00:05:11,955
- at least 30 portions of dough.
- Doh Kyung Soo!

139
00:05:12,385 --> 00:05:15,695
(The number of the dough portions is stated in the contract.)

140
00:05:15,825 --> 00:05:17,365
We settled on at least 30 and up to 40.

141
00:05:17,365 --> 00:05:19,595
- How many portions did he prep?
- Today... Ten portions, I think.

142
00:05:19,595 --> 00:05:21,265
- He prepped 10 portions today.
- More than 10 portions are left.

143
00:05:21,265 --> 00:05:23,065
Right. It's because you prepped only ten portions...

144
00:05:23,065 --> 00:05:24,265
Tomorrow, you'll only be open for lunch.

145
00:05:24,265 --> 00:05:27,235
- Exactly.
- You have ten portions left here,

146
00:05:27,235 --> 00:05:28,905
so you can use these tomorrow. It's perfect.

147
00:05:28,905 --> 00:05:30,205
- No, that's not right.
- No?

148
00:05:30,905 --> 00:05:32,675
It's clearly stated in your contract, so...

149
00:05:32,905 --> 00:05:34,115
You lost.

150
00:05:34,115 --> 00:05:35,615
Still, a deal is a deal.

151
00:05:36,245 --> 00:05:37,815
Come to think of it, we're paying you 300 dollars.

152
00:05:37,815 --> 00:05:38,985
We'll actually pay you.

153
00:05:38,985 --> 00:05:40,515
- And you'll keep your promise.
- Right.

154
00:05:40,685 --> 00:05:42,655
Let's see how many portions are left and then talk again.

155
00:05:42,655 --> 00:05:43,715
(His wishy-washy answer...)

156
00:05:43,955 --> 00:05:45,755
(sparks a massive backlash.)

157
00:05:45,755 --> 00:05:47,025
I mean, tomorrow...

158
00:05:47,725 --> 00:05:49,925
We didn't even sell ten portions today.

159
00:05:50,455 --> 00:05:52,165
(The countless emotions)

160
00:05:52,165 --> 00:05:53,565
(Floating by)

161
00:05:53,565 --> 00:05:55,795
(The serenade for the dough)

162
00:05:55,795 --> 00:05:57,035
How does the chorus part go?

163
00:05:57,265 --> 00:05:58,465
- Sorry?
- How does the chorus part go?

164
00:05:58,465 --> 00:06:00,105
- What are you talking about?
- Your song.

165
00:06:00,105 --> 00:06:01,135
- The song you just sang?
- Yes.

166
00:06:01,135 --> 00:06:02,475
(I cry sometimes)

167
00:06:02,475 --> 00:06:04,245
(I cry sometimes)

168
00:06:04,245 --> 00:06:05,905
(I laugh sometimes)

169
00:06:06,145 --> 00:06:09,045
(They sing the wrong lyrics with pure enthusiasm.)

170
00:06:09,275 --> 00:06:10,845
- I cry sometimes - I cry sometimes

171
00:06:11,045 --> 00:06:12,485
- I laugh sometimes - I laugh sometimes

172
00:06:12,745 --> 00:06:13,845
I get hurt too

173
00:06:13,845 --> 00:06:16,085
Wait. Someone can't seem to make a heart.

174
00:06:16,085 --> 00:06:17,725
- What?
- Oh, come on.

175
00:06:17,725 --> 00:06:19,625
Maybe she can't make a heart because she genuinely likes him.

176
00:06:19,625 --> 00:06:20,655
Really?

177
00:06:21,795 --> 00:06:23,425
Kyung Soo, here's what I think.

178
00:06:24,195 --> 00:06:26,695
I think I'd be like her if So Ji Sub were here.

179
00:06:26,925 --> 00:06:28,095
- Are you serious?
- Yes.

180
00:06:28,465 --> 00:06:30,535
- I would behave like Young Ji.
- Why didn't you just do it?

181
00:06:30,535 --> 00:06:31,665
- Why didn't you make a heart?
- Why...

182
00:06:31,665 --> 00:06:33,265
- I cry sometimes - That was hilarious.

183
00:06:33,565 --> 00:06:36,935
(While Young Ji feels shy, making a heart...)

184
00:06:37,235 --> 00:06:38,505
(A new party enters the restaurant.)

185
00:06:38,505 --> 00:06:39,575
Welcome.

186
00:06:40,005 --> 00:06:41,575
- Hello.
- Hello.

187
00:06:42,915 --> 00:06:45,585
- Would you like to order now?
- Yes, please.

188
00:06:45,985 --> 00:06:47,555
Feel free to look around over there...

189
00:06:47,555 --> 00:06:49,315
while you wait.

190
00:06:50,515 --> 00:06:52,785
(After guiding the customers to the waiting area...)

191
00:06:52,925 --> 00:06:55,695
Please put this on your table. Thank you.

192
00:06:55,955 --> 00:06:57,725
Why won't Cheol Yong come out?

193
00:06:57,725 --> 00:06:59,365
I'm embarrassed.

194
00:06:59,365 --> 00:07:01,665
How did you even act in the "Small Girl" music video?

195
00:07:01,765 --> 00:07:03,265
Well, back then...

196
00:07:03,935 --> 00:07:05,635
I did my best with my professional mindset.

197
00:07:06,735 --> 00:07:08,735
Try to be more lovey-dovey. Someone else...

198
00:07:08,735 --> 00:07:10,905
- Help me with hash browns please.
- Okay.

199
00:07:12,775 --> 00:07:14,475
Making me work is her ultimate weapon.

200
00:07:14,475 --> 00:07:16,245
It's basically an assassination.

201
00:07:16,245 --> 00:07:19,545
Tomorrow is our last day working together.

202
00:07:19,945 --> 00:07:22,115
- Oh, gosh. How...
- It feels so hollow.

203
00:07:22,385 --> 00:07:23,485
Are you abandoning me?

204
00:07:24,585 --> 00:07:26,455
I'm not abandoning you. Our restaurant will be gone.

205
00:07:26,925 --> 00:07:29,425
- We got a new order.
- Got it.

206
00:07:29,425 --> 00:07:31,965
One beef burger, one pizza, and one taco.

207
00:07:32,295 --> 00:07:33,365
Got it.

208
00:07:33,595 --> 00:07:36,095
One beef burger, one shrimp burger, one taco,

209
00:07:36,095 --> 00:07:38,835
two pomegranate ades, one yuzu ade, and two cakes.

210
00:07:39,005 --> 00:07:41,235
One beef burger, one shrimp burger,

211
00:07:41,505 --> 00:07:43,475
one pizza, and one taco.

212
00:07:43,475 --> 00:07:44,475
- Got it.
- Got it.

213
00:07:44,475 --> 00:07:45,675
(Order Status: 3 beef burgers, 2 shrimp burgers, )

214
00:07:45,675 --> 00:07:46,845
(3 rice cracker tacos, 2 pizzas)

215
00:07:47,075 --> 00:07:49,075
So... I have to make three portions of tacos?

216
00:07:49,375 --> 00:07:51,545
We have three portions of tacos to serve.

217
00:07:51,545 --> 00:07:53,815
- Thank you.
- Two shrimp and three beef burgers?

218
00:07:53,915 --> 00:07:54,915
Correct.

219
00:07:54,915 --> 00:07:56,585
- Is that correct?
- Yes.

220
00:07:56,755 --> 00:07:58,755
Three beef burgers and two shrimp burgers.

221
00:07:59,085 --> 00:08:00,525
Okay. Two shrimp burgers and three beef burgers.

222
00:08:00,525 --> 00:08:01,725
- Yes.
- Okay.

223
00:08:04,265 --> 00:08:08,895
(Mimi has several portions of tacos to make at the same time.)

224
00:08:09,265 --> 00:08:12,205
(Stir-frying beef with passion)

225
00:08:12,635 --> 00:08:14,935
(Putting the beef between the rice crackers)

226
00:08:19,375 --> 00:08:22,315
(Adding the toppings as the final touch)

227
00:08:22,845 --> 00:08:24,385
Three portions of tacos are up.

228
00:08:24,385 --> 00:08:25,385
(3 portions of rice cracker taco are ready!)

229
00:08:25,545 --> 00:08:27,685
- Table 13 and Table 6 ordered 1.
- Yes, 1 for Table 6.

230
00:08:27,885 --> 00:08:29,255
- This is for Table 13.
- Okay.

231
00:08:29,255 --> 00:08:30,755
- Table 13.
- For each of Table 13 and Table 6.

232
00:08:31,155 --> 00:08:32,955
Here's your food.

233
00:08:33,785 --> 00:08:35,995
And this is coriander pesto.

234
00:08:36,295 --> 00:08:37,295
Please enjoy.

235
00:08:37,355 --> 00:08:39,825
(Cleared orders: 1 beef burger, 2 rice cracker tacos, 1 pizza)

236
00:08:40,125 --> 00:08:42,395
- One more taco is up.
- Okay.

237
00:08:42,965 --> 00:08:45,435
(Yu Jin is serving the last portion of tacos.)

238
00:08:46,165 --> 00:08:47,265
I'll just trust you.

239
00:08:47,605 --> 00:08:50,575
- Here are your tacos.
- The tacos already came out...

240
00:08:51,445 --> 00:08:53,975
(Blinking)

241
00:08:54,915 --> 00:08:55,915
Please enjoy.

242
00:08:57,115 --> 00:08:59,215
(The rice cracker taco went off track.)

243
00:09:00,045 --> 00:09:01,515
(Sighing in embarrassment)

244
00:09:01,515 --> 00:09:03,555
Why have their tacos already been served?

245
00:09:04,425 --> 00:09:07,055
But it was for Table 13.

246
00:09:08,825 --> 00:09:10,295
(Staring)

247
00:09:12,125 --> 00:09:13,925
They ordered two cakes.

248
00:09:14,635 --> 00:09:16,865
