296
00:11:12,685 --> 00:11:14,585
- Hello.
- Hello.

297
00:11:15,155 --> 00:11:17,625
- Here's your beef burger.
- Thank you.

298
00:11:17,625 --> 00:11:19,155
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

299
00:11:19,855 --> 00:11:22,095
Hello. I'm not used to finding a table number.

300
00:11:22,495 --> 00:11:23,825
You'll see me wandering around.

301
00:11:26,795 --> 00:11:28,365
Oh, this isn't the right table.

302
00:11:29,035 --> 00:11:30,495
Where am I?

303
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:32,705
Oh, no. I have to go back that way.

304
00:11:32,705 --> 00:11:34,065
(Passing through)

305
00:11:34,275 --> 00:11:35,605
Enjoy your meal.

306
00:11:36,475 --> 00:11:37,675
(She enters the secondary hall.)

307
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:40,245
- Oh, my. Hello.
- Hello.

308
00:11:40,245 --> 00:11:42,375
Here's your beef burger.

309
00:11:43,515 --> 00:11:44,645
Do you like the food?

310
00:11:44,645 --> 00:11:46,445
- It's delicious.
- Please enjoy.

311
00:11:47,085 --> 00:11:49,585
(Two beef burgers have been served.)

312
00:11:49,755 --> 00:11:52,225
(All orders have been cleared!)

313
00:11:52,725 --> 00:11:55,055
(As the evening deepens, )

314
00:11:55,695 --> 00:11:58,095
(the ingredients begin to run low.)

315
00:11:58,095 --> 00:12:00,295
Basil... Mozzarella.

316
00:12:00,295 --> 00:12:01,535
(The ingredients begin to run low.)

317
00:12:01,535 --> 00:12:02,565
Mozzarella.

318
00:12:03,165 --> 00:12:05,665
(Empty)

319
00:12:08,135 --> 00:12:10,475
- Can I ask you just one favor?
- Pizza and rice cracker taco...

320
00:12:11,205 --> 00:12:13,245
- Can you make some of this?
- There's nothing left? Of course.

321
00:12:13,345 --> 00:12:14,375
Thank you.

322
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:17,885
(While she's refilling the tomato salsa...)

323
00:12:18,415 --> 00:12:21,215
(This is not fast-forwarded.)

324
00:12:21,515 --> 00:12:23,785
(Director Doh made it in a flash.)

325
00:12:23,785 --> 00:12:26,725
- Here you go.
- My gosh. You're the best, Master.

326
00:12:28,025 --> 00:12:29,095
He may seem aloof on the outside, but he's actually so caring.

327
00:12:31,365 --> 00:12:32,395
He's so caring.

328
00:12:32,395 --> 00:12:33,965
(Master has a sharp tongue, but he grants their every wish.)

329
00:12:34,495 --> 00:12:36,895
(He takes the final party's order.)

330
00:12:36,895 --> 00:12:37,905
Yes.

331
00:12:37,905 --> 00:12:39,765
One taco, one pizza,

332
00:12:40,505 --> 00:12:41,505
and one shrimp burger.

333
00:12:41,675 --> 00:12:44,775
Let's do our best until we clear the final party's order.

334
00:12:44,775 --> 00:12:46,145
- Let's do this!
- Let's do this!

335
00:12:47,205 --> 00:12:48,975
- Here goes Master's sauce.
- We've got this.

336
00:12:49,445 --> 00:12:50,675
Shut down

337
00:12:51,415 --> 00:12:54,555
(So they've finished making today's last dishes.)

338
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:55,915
Hello.

339
00:12:55,915 --> 00:12:57,485
(Table 1: 1 shrimp burger combo)

340
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:58,555
Here are your tacos.

341
00:12:59,185 --> 00:13:00,385
Thank you.

342
00:13:00,725 --> 00:13:02,355
- Thank you for your patience.
- Thank you.

343
00:13:02,355 --> 00:13:03,425
(Table 1: All orders are cleared.)

344
00:13:03,755 --> 00:13:06,265
Ghost pepper...

345
00:13:07,695 --> 00:13:10,195
Here's your ghost pepper pizza. Please excuse my pronunciation.

346
00:13:10,435 --> 00:13:11,905
Please enjoy.

347
00:13:12,835 --> 00:13:14,675
Good job, everyone.

348
00:13:14,775 --> 00:13:16,105
- Good job.
- Good job.

349
00:13:16,475 --> 00:13:18,975
(The head chef, who doesn't feel rushed anymore...)

350
00:13:19,175 --> 00:13:20,405
- Are you enjoying the food?
- Yes, it's delicious.

351
00:13:20,405 --> 00:13:22,575
- How was the burger?
- I really enjoyed it.

352
00:13:22,575 --> 00:13:24,015
Was there no problem at all?

353
00:13:24,315 --> 00:13:25,715
(It's delicious.)

354
00:13:25,945 --> 00:13:27,215
How is everything with your burgers?

355
00:13:27,445 --> 00:13:28,885
- It's really good.
- I finished my burger.

356
00:13:29,215 --> 00:13:30,255
Thank you.

357
00:13:30,255 --> 00:13:32,185
(The second rice cake burger got positive feedback, fortunately.)

358
00:13:32,985 --> 00:13:34,125
(Bowing)

359
00:13:34,285 --> 00:13:36,095
- The tteokbokki...
- Pardon me?

360
00:13:36,255 --> 00:13:37,925
- The tteokbokki...
- It was so exhausting.

361
00:13:38,325 --> 00:13:39,595
So we took it off the menu just for today.

362
00:13:39,595 --> 00:13:40,625
(Disappointed)

363
00:13:40,865 --> 00:13:43,035
We're planning to serve it tomorrow.

364
00:13:43,035 --> 00:13:46,705
Instead, this rice cracker taco was Director Doh Kyung Soo's idea...

365
00:13:46,805 --> 00:13:49,375
- "Director?"
- Is he? I'm not sure.

366
00:13:49,535 --> 00:13:52,775
Anyway, he came up with this recipe.

367
00:13:54,145 --> 00:13:55,145
Try it.

368
00:13:56,615 --> 00:13:59,285
(While everyone is enjoying the food...)

369
00:13:59,485 --> 00:14:00,785
Excuse me.

370
00:14:00,785 --> 00:14:02,185
(A customer secretly approaches the counter.)

371
00:14:02,455 --> 00:14:04,885
Tomorrow is the birthday of someone in our party.

372
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:06,385
Is it okay for us to bring out a cake at our table?

373
00:14:06,385 --> 00:14:08,755
- Of course. Absolutely.
- Okay.

374
00:14:08,755 --> 00:14:11,425
- Thank you. It's 13.
- What is your table number?

375
00:14:11,425 --> 00:14:12,765
- Okay. Table 13?
- Yes.

376
00:14:13,895 --> 00:14:15,335
(He returns with an excited look on his face.)

377
00:14:15,335 --> 00:14:18,705
People at Table 13 are celebrating the birthday of 1 of them.

378
00:14:18,705 --> 00:14:19,735
A birthday at Table 13?

379
00:14:20,165 --> 00:14:22,535
Table 13 is celebrating 1 of their birthdays.

380
00:14:22,975 --> 00:14:25,605
She asked me if they could bring out a cake at their table.

381
00:14:25,605 --> 00:14:28,575
Kyung Soo looks like he's actually working here.

382
00:14:28,975 --> 00:14:31,745
- Are we giving a performance?
- Shall we? What do you say?

383
00:14:31,885 --> 00:14:33,485
I kind of want to do it.

384
00:14:33,745 --> 00:14:36,615
(The customers have finished their food.)

385
00:14:37,085 --> 00:14:39,285
(And they bring out the birthday cake.)

386
00:14:39,285 --> 00:14:40,325
It's so cute.

387
00:14:40,555 --> 00:14:42,925
- They're bringing out the cake.
- We should celebrate...

388
00:14:42,925 --> 00:14:44,695
- The cake celebration is starting.
- I see.

389
00:14:45,095 --> 00:14:46,365
- Let's go.
- The cake they brought here?

390
00:14:46,565 --> 00:14:48,265
(Nervous)

391
00:14:48,565 --> 00:14:49,835
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

392
00:14:50,835 --> 00:14:53,165
(Led by the party planner, )

393
00:14:53,565 --> 00:14:55,605
(they make their entrance in a single line.)

394
00:14:56,075 --> 00:14:58,375
(Meanwhile, the birthday table has no idea what's coming for them.)

395
00:14:58,645 --> 00:15:00,675
How about we sing the song silently?

396
00:15:00,945 --> 00:15:02,015
Should we just clap?

397
00:15:02,415 --> 00:15:05,445
- Let's go with "Popcorn."
- Okay.

398
00:15:05,445 --> 00:15:06,445
(They secretly chose the song to sing.)

399
00:15:06,715 --> 00:15:09,355
- Just like the day we first met - Just like the day we first met

400
00:15:09,685 --> 00:15:13,555
- Looking at you makes me happy - Looking at you makes me happy

401
00:15:13,555 --> 00:15:16,955
(They slowly surround the table.)

402
00:15:17,255 --> 00:15:21,165
(Puzzled)

403
00:15:21,535 --> 00:15:23,195
Congratulations.

404
00:15:23,195 --> 00:15:24,835
I heard today is one of your birthdays.

405
00:15:25,235 --> 00:15:26,905
(That's me.)

406
00:15:26,905 --> 00:15:28,735
- By any chance...
- Do you have a match?

407
00:15:28,735 --> 00:15:30,335
Let me do it for you.

408
00:15:30,635 --> 00:15:32,445
(Covering her mouth)

409
00:15:32,445 --> 00:15:35,675
You need to be careful. Please be careful.

410
00:15:35,675 --> 00:15:36,875
The flowers might catch fire.

411
00:15:37,075 --> 00:15:39,545
- Let me...
- "Let me do it for you."

412
00:15:39,545 --> 00:15:41,215
- Start with the instrumental intro.
- Please be careful.

413
00:15:41,215 --> 00:15:42,955
- The flowers might catch fire.
- This song? Congratulations

414
00:15:42,955 --> 00:15:44,185
(Yes, that's the song.)

415
00:15:44,755 --> 00:15:47,385
- It's the air conditioner...
- Because of the breeze from it...

416
00:15:47,525 --> 00:15:48,795
Gosh, my finger.

417
00:15:48,795 --> 00:15:50,795
(Singing)

418
00:15:50,795 --> 00:15:51,995
(Singing)

419
00:15:52,225 --> 00:15:54,865
(They start their performance just as they discussed.)

420
00:15:54,965 --> 00:15:56,265
(Chanting)

421
00:15:56,665 --> 00:15:58,905
(Happy birthday to you)

422
00:15:59,105 --> 00:16:00,135
(Hey!)

423
00:16:00,605 --> 00:16:01,775
(In the zone)

424
00:16:02,135 --> 00:16:03,705
(They're using the celebration as an excuse to have fun.)

425
00:16:03,975 --> 00:16:06,405
(Happy birthday to you)

426
00:16:06,645 --> 00:16:08,375
(Singing)

427
00:16:09,215 --> 00:16:10,575
Please stand up.

428
00:16:11,045 --> 00:16:12,585
- Happy birthday.
- Please stand on the chair.

429
00:16:12,585 --> 00:16:14,045
- Go ahead.
- Why stand on the chair?

430
00:16:14,315 --> 00:16:15,385
- Please stand on the chair.
- Why?

431
00:16:16,155 --> 00:16:18,285
- Watch your head.
- Say a word to your friends.

432
00:16:18,285 --> 00:16:20,855
Thank you for giving me the chance to celebrate my birthday like this.

433
00:16:22,025 --> 00:16:23,755
Happy birthday!

434
00:16:23,925 --> 00:16:25,895
Everyone, wish her a happy birthday. Ready, go.

435
00:16:25,895 --> 00:16:29,395
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday!

436
00:16:30,295 --> 00:16:31,935
Blow out the candle.

437
00:16:32,265 --> 00:16:33,465
(Blowing)

438
00:16:34,035 --> 00:16:35,305
(People in the back are celebrating as well.)

439
00:16:35,535 --> 00:16:37,175
- Thank you.
- My goodness.

440
00:16:37,375 --> 00:16:38,405
- Just like the day - We will...

441
00:16:38,805 --> 00:16:41,375
We will continue to do our best at Space Rice Cake!

442
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:44,245
- We are sincerely grateful.
- Thank you.

443
00:16:44,245 --> 00:16:45,315
(Bowing together amid the cheers)

444
00:16:45,685 --> 00:16:48,355
- Just like the day we first met - Just like the day we first met

445
00:16:48,455 --> 00:16:51,855
(They wrap it up by singing the exit song they messed up earlier.)

446
00:16:51,855 --> 00:16:53,385
(I forgot about being nervous...)

447
00:16:53,385 --> 00:16:54,555
Fade out.

448
00:16:55,625 --> 00:16:59,265
(Leaving the stage as a full circle)

449
00:16:59,495 --> 00:17:02,295
(The performance team returning with a sense of pride)

450
00:17:02,765 --> 00:17:05,435
(A lasting impression)

451
00:17:05,435 --> 00:17:07,105
- I'll never forget it.
- Right.

452
00:17:07,605 --> 00:17:09,335
They kept making interjections...

453
00:17:09,335 --> 00:17:10,535
Put that on top of this.

454
00:17:10,605 --> 00:17:12,905
(The table that paid again is leaving after finishing their food.)

455
00:17:12,905 --> 00:17:14,075
Hello.

456
00:17:14,075 --> 00:17:15,245
I heard that your beef burger...

457
00:17:15,245 --> 00:17:16,415
- wasn't fully cooked.
- It was okay.

458
00:17:16,415 --> 00:17:18,645
- I'm so sorry. We will cancel...
- We ate it.

459
00:17:18,645 --> 00:17:20,345
- that order.
- No, it's okay.

460
00:17:20,345 --> 00:17:22,885
If we don't do that, Chef Young Ji won't be...

461
00:17:22,885 --> 00:17:24,985
- able to sleep tonight.
- She won't be able to sleep.

462
00:17:24,985 --> 00:17:27,325
- Let me handle that fast.
- Right.

463
00:17:27,325 --> 00:17:28,525
I'm extremely fast.

464
00:17:28,525 --> 00:17:29,755
If not, you can't leave.

465
00:17:29,755 --> 00:17:31,025
Right. We'll block your way out.

466
00:17:31,465 --> 00:17:34,095
(Starting with customers who had to pay again, )

467
00:17:34,395 --> 00:17:37,335
(customers head out, 1 by 1.)

468
00:17:37,495 --> 00:17:38,835
What was your favorite?

469
00:17:39,205 --> 00:17:40,335
- The carrot cake.
- The carrot cake.

470
00:17:42,875 --> 00:17:43,905
Thank you.

471
00:17:43,905 --> 00:17:44,975
(Stomping her feet with joy)

472
00:17:45,205 --> 00:17:46,875
It wasn't intentional.

473
00:17:47,805 --> 00:17:49,815
Guys, are a lot of people gone from the second floor?

474
00:17:49,815 --> 00:17:50,845
Then we need to bring the dishes downstairs.

475
00:17:50,845 --> 00:17:52,085
- I'll bring them down.
- Okay.

476
00:17:53,145 --> 00:17:55,185
(Young Ji and Kyung Soo head up to the 2nd floor.)

477
00:17:55,355 --> 00:17:56,385
(Mimi follows right behind them.)

478
00:17:56,385 --> 00:17:57,985
- Is the tray over there?
- Go.

479
00:17:58,155 --> 00:17:59,725
I should let those two go alone...

480
00:18:00,455 --> 00:18:01,495
and enjoy some time together.

481
00:18:01,595 --> 00:18:02,595
(Shrieking with joy)

482
00:18:02,595 --> 00:18:03,695
That's right, Mimi.

483
00:18:03,695 --> 00:18:06,465
I almost third wheeled them. That was clueless of me.

484
00:18:06,465 --> 00:18:09,095
- Why did you do that?
- I almost third wheeled them.

485
00:18:09,095 --> 00:18:11,365
- I know.
- They were walking side by side.

486
00:18:11,365 --> 00:18:13,835
We never had romance at our workplace.

487
00:18:13,835 --> 00:18:15,135
When I said that...

488
00:18:15,135 --> 00:18:17,035
someone needs to go up to the second floor,

489
00:18:17,035 --> 00:18:18,275
Kyung Soo went up. Young Ji followed right behind him.

490
00:18:18,775 --> 00:18:19,775
(Rumors being made in real time)

491
00:18:19,775 --> 00:18:21,475
- There's something going on.
- Definitely.

492
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:23,145
There has to be one.

493
00:18:23,145 --> 00:18:24,145
Exactly.

494
00:18:24,345 --> 00:18:28,815
(In reality, everyone is diligently minding their own business.)

495
00:18:29,085 --> 00:18:32,025
(Kyung Soo returns with both hands full.)

496
00:18:32,185 --> 00:18:33,385
- Kyung Soo.
- Yes?

497
00:18:33,385 --> 00:18:35,355
Do you want one of us to help you upstairs?

498
00:18:35,625 --> 00:18:36,725
No, it's okay.

499
00:18:37,625 --> 00:18:39,595
(Smiling mischievously)

500
00:18:39,695 --> 00:18:41,395
- What?
- It's nothing.

501
00:18:41,395 --> 00:18:43,095
- It's nothing.
- See you later.

502
00:18:43,095 --> 00:18:44,395
(Something feels off.)

503
00:18:44,935 --> 00:18:48,005
- See? I told you.
- There's something going on.

504
00:18:48,005 --> 00:18:49,935
- I was right.
- Goodness.

505
00:18:52,545 --> 00:18:54,445
(They're clearly going their separate ways.)

506
00:18:55,045 --> 00:18:56,745
- What's going on?
- Nothing.

507
00:18:57,445 --> 00:18:58,785
- It's nothing.
- Well done.

508
00:18:58,785 --> 00:19:00,015
- Tell me what's going on.
- Good job.

509
00:19:00,015 --> 00:19:01,485
Young Ji, is there a lot in the pantry?

510
00:19:01,955 --> 00:19:03,715
I think there's more in the pantry on the second floor.

511
00:19:03,715 --> 00:19:05,025
- Okay.
- Young Ji.

512
00:19:05,025 --> 00:19:06,385
Do you want one of us to go up instead?

513
00:19:06,385 --> 00:19:07,485
No, I'll go.

514
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:09,425
(Smiling)

515
00:19:09,425 --> 00:19:11,625
(Exchanging sneaky little smiles)

516
00:19:11,825 --> 00:19:14,265
- Go ahead.
- Go on.

517
00:19:14,595 --> 00:19:16,395
- Go on.
- Go and work.

518
00:19:16,395 --> 00:19:17,395
(The head chef is pushed out of the kitchen.)

519
00:19:17,735 --> 00:19:20,235
(Feeling suspicious, she takes a step back.)

520
00:19:20,705 --> 00:19:23,135
(She told us not to come up.)

521
00:19:23,135 --> 00:19:24,375
She told us not to come up.

522
00:19:26,875 --> 00:19:29,475
You two bring everything down, okay?

523
00:19:30,515 --> 00:19:31,585
Just the two of you.

524
00:19:32,885 --> 00:19:35,215
(Speechless)

525
00:19:35,485 --> 00:19:38,425
(Young Ji tidies up the pantry by herself.)

526
00:19:38,555 --> 00:19:39,725
(She returns to the kitchen.)

527
00:19:39,725 --> 00:19:41,285
- You're back.
- You're back.

528
00:19:41,595 --> 00:19:43,655
- Thank you.
- Well done.

529
00:19:43,825 --> 00:19:44,865
What's going on?

530
00:19:44,865 --> 00:19:46,825
- It's nothing.
- You two work so hard.

531
00:19:46,825 --> 00:19:47,925
Take them to the dishwashing room.

532
00:19:47,925 --> 00:19:48,965
Were you saying something weird?

533
00:19:48,965 --> 00:19:50,395
- No.
- No way.

534
00:19:50,595 --> 00:19:52,405
Did she go upstairs again?

535
00:19:52,405 --> 00:19:53,565
No, not yet.

536
00:19:55,635 --> 00:19:57,775
(The workaholic heads upstairs again.)

537
00:20:00,245 --> 00:20:02,845
She's never gone upstairs this whole time...

538
00:20:02,845 --> 00:20:04,945
- we've been running our business.
- I know.

539
00:20:05,815 --> 00:20:07,245
It's done.

540
00:20:07,245 --> 00:20:08,815
There's more in the pantry on the second floor.

541
00:20:09,115 --> 00:20:10,115
Honesty.

542
00:20:10,115 --> 00:20:12,385
- Humility. Ahk.
- Humility. Ahk.

543
00:20:13,255 --> 00:20:15,655
- Isn't Kyung Soo going home?
- He should.

544
00:20:15,725 --> 00:20:18,025
- Tell him to go home.
- We should send him home first.

545
00:20:18,025 --> 00:20:19,025
Send who?

546
00:20:19,265 --> 00:20:20,795
- Kyung Soo here.
- Send who home?

547
00:20:20,795 --> 00:20:21,935
- Kyung Soo.
- Thank you for your work,

548
00:20:21,935 --> 00:20:23,495
- Kyung Soo.
- Kyung Soo, are you really leaving?

549
00:20:23,495 --> 00:20:24,665
But Kyung Soo...

550
00:20:26,105 --> 00:20:27,435
(Bowing)

551
00:20:27,435 --> 00:20:29,335
Shouldn't we at least hear...

552
00:20:29,335 --> 00:20:30,805
how it went for him today?

553
00:20:30,805 --> 00:20:31,905
It was fun.

554
00:20:32,305 --> 00:20:33,545
- That's all?
- "It was fun."

555
00:20:34,105 --> 00:20:35,115
If...

556
00:20:35,115 --> 00:20:36,915
If we do something like this again, will you come back?

557
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:38,945
I'll come back.

558
00:20:39,385 --> 00:20:40,745
(They're surprised by his positive answer.)

559
00:20:40,745 --> 00:20:42,085
- When will you do it?
- Tomorrow.

560
00:20:42,085 --> 00:20:43,885
- Tomorrow.
- I have to go to Macao tomorrow.

561
00:20:44,455 --> 00:20:45,485
I can't come back tomorrow.

562
00:20:45,785 --> 00:20:47,425
If you do it again later, I'll come back.

563
00:20:47,425 --> 00:20:48,425
- That sounds good.
- That sounds good.

564
00:20:48,425 --> 00:20:49,425
(We will remember that.)

565
00:20:49,425 --> 00:20:50,495
Next time.

566
00:20:50,495 --> 00:20:51,825
It's downstairs in the safe.

567
00:20:51,825 --> 00:20:52,965
- Really?
- Yes.

568
00:20:52,965 --> 00:20:53,965
Three hundred dollars?

569
00:20:54,225 --> 00:20:55,565
Do we give him all of this?

570
00:20:56,395 --> 00:20:58,635
Ten, fifteen...

571
00:20:58,635 --> 00:20:59,665
(When it's time to pay him, it's hard to share the earnings.)

572
00:20:59,965 --> 00:21:02,705
(She still carefully tucks it into an envelope.)

573
00:21:02,905 --> 00:21:04,605
Your pay in advance... Goodness.

574
00:21:04,605 --> 00:21:05,605
Gosh.

575
00:21:05,605 --> 00:21:07,005
- You're fast.
- He's ready to leave.

576
00:21:07,005 --> 00:21:09,145
He even took off his microphone.

577
00:21:09,145 --> 00:21:11,075
(Leaving behind his clothes and microphone)

578
00:21:11,075 --> 00:21:12,345
Take your money before you go.

579
00:21:12,685 --> 00:21:15,015
He even took off the microphone. I feel hurt, Kyung Soo.

580
00:21:15,885 --> 00:21:17,715
- Well done.
- Thank you.

581
00:21:17,715 --> 00:21:18,725
It's for your part-time work.

582
00:21:19,085 --> 00:21:20,855
- Thank you. Well done.
- Thank you so much.

583
00:21:20,855 --> 00:21:22,725
Thank you, Mr. Part-Timer.

584
00:21:22,725 --> 00:21:24,865
- Well done. Good luck.
- See you again.

585
00:21:24,865 --> 00:21:25,865
(He doesn't have a microphone.)

586
00:21:25,865 --> 00:21:27,695
We'll walk you out to the door.

587
00:21:28,125 --> 00:21:29,995
- Let's walk him out.
- Doh Kyung Soo.

588
00:21:29,995 --> 00:21:30,995
- Leave it anywhere.
- Hey.

589
00:21:30,995 --> 00:21:32,905
- Doh Kyung Soo.
- Hey.

590
00:21:32,905 --> 00:21:34,905
- Doh Kyung Soo.
- Hey.

591
00:21:34,905 --> 00:21:36,835
- Thank you, Kyung Soo.
- Doh Kyung Soo.

592
00:21:36,835 --> 00:21:38,775
- Doh Kyung Soo.
- Hey.

593
00:21:38,775 --> 00:21:40,645
- Take care.
- Doh Kyung Soo.

594
00:21:40,645 --> 00:21:41,775
Doh Kyung...

595
00:21:41,775 --> 00:21:42,775
Let's hurry and prep.

596
00:21:42,915 --> 00:21:43,915
Let's prep quickly.

597
00:21:44,015 --> 00:21:45,745
(Current time, 9:06pm)

598
00:21:45,745 --> 00:21:46,745
Let's do our work.

599
00:21:46,745 --> 00:21:48,455
He practically threw it away.

600
00:21:48,685 --> 00:21:49,755
(The uniform he shed on his way out)

601
00:21:49,755 --> 00:21:50,915
He must've really hated it.

602
00:21:51,385 --> 00:21:52,985
It must've been exhausting.

603
00:21:52,985 --> 00:21:54,685
I guess he had a really tough time.

604
00:21:54,685 --> 00:21:56,155
He even took off his microphone.

605
00:21:56,155 --> 00:21:57,195
He must've been...

606
00:21:57,325 --> 00:21:59,225
desperate to get out of here fast.

607
00:21:59,765 --> 00:22:01,225
Today's sales.

608
00:22:01,995 --> 00:22:03,165
- Today's sales.
- Okay.

609
00:22:03,495 --> 00:22:04,495
What's the amount?

610
00:22:04,495 --> 00:22:05,505
It's...

611
00:22:05,935 --> 00:22:07,305
It's 2,109.5 dollars.

612
00:22:08,605 --> 00:22:10,475
We earned 50 more dollars today.

613
00:22:10,475 --> 00:22:11,475
(2,000 dollars in sales again today)

614
00:22:11,475 --> 00:22:12,875
- That's amazing.
- That's amazing.

615
00:22:12,875 --> 00:22:14,075
How much did we pay Kyung Soo?

616
00:22:14,075 --> 00:22:15,075
We paid him 300 dollars.

617
00:22:15,075 --> 00:22:17,545
- Right.
- His work was worth more than that.

618
00:22:17,545 --> 00:22:20,215
- He went above and beyond.
- Definitely.

619
00:22:20,385 --> 00:22:22,255
(Today's sales)

620
00:22:22,255 --> 00:22:23,385
(27 beef burger combos, 24 shrimp burger combos, )

621
00:22:23,385 --> 00:22:24,655
(34 rice cracker tacos, 22 ghost pepper pizzas...)

622
00:22:24,755 --> 00:22:27,155
(Total sales, 2,109.5 dollars)

623
00:22:27,155 --> 00:22:28,625
We hit...

624
00:22:28,755 --> 00:22:30,395
another all-time sales record.

625
00:22:30,395 --> 00:22:31,455
We made the most ever.

626
00:22:31,695 --> 00:22:32,925
It's all thanks to you.

627
00:22:32,925 --> 00:22:34,565
- Honesty.
- It's thanks to you. Humility.

628
00:22:34,565 --> 00:22:37,195
- Ahk.
- Ahk.

629
00:22:37,195 --> 00:22:38,235
(Stronger bonds thanks to record-breaking sales)

630
00:22:38,235 --> 00:22:39,535
Let's hurry up with the prep and clean up.

631
00:22:39,535 --> 00:22:41,905
- Let's go.
- I have to make dough and sauce.

632
00:22:41,905 --> 00:22:43,105
This is insane.

633
00:22:43,105 --> 00:22:45,605
(Back to reality with a mountain of work waiting)

634
00:22:45,805 --> 00:22:47,945
What do you have to prepare? Let's start with Eun Ji.

635
00:22:47,945 --> 00:22:50,615
Tteokramisu and carrot cupcakes.

636
00:22:50,615 --> 00:22:53,545
All I have to do is cut some jeolpyeon...

637
00:22:53,545 --> 00:22:54,585
- Jeolpyeon and...
- and dough.

638
00:22:54,585 --> 00:22:56,015
Then you should make the dough.

639
00:22:56,015 --> 00:22:57,655
I'll prepare the seasoning paste.

640
00:22:57,655 --> 00:23:00,455
(Why dishes from Goheung all of a sudden?)

641
00:23:00,455 --> 00:23:02,095
It doesn't matter as long as there's pizza.

642
00:23:02,095 --> 00:23:03,355
Let's make the entire...

643
00:23:03,355 --> 00:23:04,625
- previous menu tomorrow.
- Pollack roe...

644
00:23:04,625 --> 00:23:06,165
- Tomorrow is our last day.
- But we won't say the names.

645
00:23:06,165 --> 00:23:08,665
(At the head chef's command)

646
00:23:08,665 --> 00:23:10,065
(Tteokbokki, beef burger, shrimp burger, rice cake pasta, )

647
00:23:10,065 --> 00:23:12,005
(pizza, carrot cake, tteokramisu, pomegranate ade, yuzu ade)

648
00:23:12,105 --> 00:23:15,105
(They'll make all these dishes because tomorrow is the last day.)

649
00:23:15,105 --> 00:23:18,175
(That's why they have a huge amount of work.)

650
00:23:18,305 --> 00:23:19,345
(They remember to stay clean.)

651
00:23:19,345 --> 00:23:21,005
There's so much work that I don't know where to start.

652
00:23:21,005 --> 00:23:22,715
Wash your hands.

653
00:23:23,315 --> 00:23:25,885
Soon, this will be part of our memory.

654
00:23:26,585 --> 00:23:29,055
- This is our last prep.
- It's our last prep.

655
00:23:29,055 --> 00:23:30,555
No, there's tomorrow morning.

656
00:23:30,555 --> 00:23:31,615
It feels strange.

657
00:23:31,615 --> 00:23:34,055
(With last day to go, they feel a mix of emotions.)

658
00:23:34,055 --> 00:23:35,555
I'll start with the chestnut cream.

659
00:23:35,725 --> 00:23:36,995
Yes, chestnut cream.

660
00:23:36,995 --> 00:23:38,625
I haven't made chestnut cream in a while.

661
00:23:38,625 --> 00:23:39,995
- Right.
- Hasn't it been a long time?

662
00:23:39,995 --> 00:23:41,025
Yes.

663
00:23:41,025 --> 00:23:42,265
Please make it delicious.

664
00:23:42,265 --> 00:23:44,495
We started by making this, didn't we?

665
00:23:44,495 --> 00:23:45,535
- Right.
- We did.

666
00:23:45,535 --> 00:23:46,565
That was the original dish.

667
00:23:46,565 --> 00:23:47,735
(The last night is suddenly filled with nostalgia.)

668
00:23:47,735 --> 00:23:49,705
- It's making me cry.
- Why?

669
00:23:49,705 --> 00:23:51,805
Tomorrow is really our last day.

670
00:23:52,245 --> 00:23:54,875
Young Ji, I'll start by chopping green onions.

671
00:23:54,875 --> 00:23:56,745
(Save the reminiscing for later. Prep comes first.)

672
00:23:56,745 --> 00:23:57,845
I love you.

673
00:23:58,885 --> 00:24:00,085
Please respond.

674
00:24:00,085 --> 00:24:01,345
I love you, Cheol Yong.

675
00:24:02,685 --> 00:24:03,715
Junghye.

676
00:24:03,715 --> 00:24:04,755
(Now that he's gone, Cheol Yong appears.)

677
00:24:04,755 --> 00:24:06,025
Where have you been?

678
00:24:06,025 --> 00:24:08,085
I've been looking for you, Cheol Yong.

679
00:24:08,085 --> 00:24:10,655
I told you that we're dating in secret.

680
00:24:10,895 --> 00:24:13,225
Earlier, you kept saying we had to meet in secret.

681
00:24:13,225 --> 00:24:15,465
So I thought something was going on.

682
00:24:15,465 --> 00:24:17,735
Today was scarier...

683
00:24:17,735 --> 00:24:19,805
than the movie "Salmokji."

684
00:24:19,935 --> 00:24:22,375
When you were looking for Cheol Yong in me.

685
00:24:23,205 --> 00:24:24,735
Cheol Yong barely made...

686
00:24:25,075 --> 00:24:26,905
his appearance today.

687
00:24:26,905 --> 00:24:29,415
I didn't have any time to be Cheol Yong today.

688
00:24:29,575 --> 00:24:31,115
I'm your fan, Cheol Yong.

689
00:24:31,375 --> 00:24:33,015
I like Junghye.

690
00:24:33,415 --> 00:24:34,485
What about me?

691
00:24:34,985 --> 00:24:35,985
Who are you?

692
00:24:36,515 --> 00:24:38,755
- I'm Jihye.
- Who?

693
00:24:38,755 --> 00:24:39,885
(Starting a love affair drama)

694
00:24:40,455 --> 00:24:41,925
Aren't we in completely different age groups?

695
00:24:41,925 --> 00:24:43,695
The name Jihye suits you well.

696
00:24:43,695 --> 00:24:44,755
I'm Jihye.

697
00:24:45,525 --> 00:24:48,865
I just made the last batch of the seasoning paste.

698
00:24:48,865 --> 00:24:49,995
(The last batch of Lee Young Ji's tteokbokki is ready.)

699
00:24:49,995 --> 00:24:51,265
It came out well.

700
00:24:51,905 --> 00:24:53,965
How does it taste?

701
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:57,175
I have to use a plastic glove, right?

702
00:24:57,375 --> 00:24:58,905
It's the taste of Goheung.

703
00:24:59,305 --> 00:25:01,375
- Does it?
- It's the taste of Goheung. Try it.

704
00:25:02,715 --> 00:25:04,345
It tastes like what we had in Goheung.

705
00:25:04,345 --> 00:25:05,715
(Getting choked up)

706
00:25:05,715 --> 00:25:07,085
(The youngest also takes a bite.)

707
00:25:07,085 --> 00:25:08,115
It's the taste of Goheung.

708
00:25:08,115 --> 00:25:09,855
(She agrees that it's the taste of Goheung.)

709
00:25:09,855 --> 00:25:10,855
This is it.

710
00:25:10,985 --> 00:25:13,485
This tteokbokki is going to make you cry.

711
00:25:14,285 --> 00:25:17,195
(Chef Mimi tastes it too.)

712
00:25:17,195 --> 00:25:19,665
(And there come the tears)

713
00:25:21,095 --> 00:25:22,095
It's the taste of Goheung.

714
00:25:22,095 --> 00:25:23,995
- Father.
- "Father?"

715
00:25:24,535 --> 00:25:26,235
- Father.
- "Father?"

716
00:25:26,235 --> 00:25:28,065
This is the taste of Goheung.

717
00:25:28,105 --> 00:25:30,275
(A taste of the sauce brings all the memories flooding back.)

718
00:25:30,275 --> 00:25:33,305
How is it? The last batch of Lee Young Ji's seasoning paste.

719
00:25:33,375 --> 00:25:35,275
Can't we eat it at your house?

720
00:25:35,715 --> 00:25:36,715
Junghye.

721
00:25:36,715 --> 00:25:37,945
(Junghye is being cold and brutally honest.)

722
00:25:37,945 --> 00:25:39,045
Cheol Yong.

723
00:25:39,045 --> 00:25:41,415
Junghye, I missed you.

724
00:25:41,415 --> 00:25:42,685
I'll start by making the dough.

725
00:25:43,785 --> 00:25:45,185
- Eun Ji.
- Yes?

726
00:25:45,185 --> 00:25:46,985
- I have a question for you.
- What?

727
00:25:46,985 --> 00:25:49,155
- Are you tired of us?
- No.

728
00:25:49,595 --> 00:25:50,925
So why are you trying to get out of the team dinner?

729
00:25:50,925 --> 00:25:51,965
I mean...

730
00:25:51,965 --> 00:25:53,325
(She got caught.)

731
00:25:53,725 --> 00:25:55,065
- You didn't look too keen.
- That's not true.

732
00:25:55,065 --> 00:25:56,735
I said I was going to the dinner.

733
00:25:57,235 --> 00:25:58,295
But you don't seem like you want to.

734
00:25:58,295 --> 00:26:00,005
We're having our team dinner. Who said that we weren't?

735
00:26:00,605 --> 00:26:02,375
You look unhappy about it.

736
00:26:02,375 --> 00:26:04,605
What do you mean? I want to stay up...

737
00:26:04,605 --> 00:26:06,345
- all night with you girls.
- Right?

738
00:26:06,345 --> 00:26:08,245
- Of course.
- I thought so.

739
00:26:08,245 --> 00:26:09,475
It'd make me insanely happy.

740
00:26:09,775 --> 00:26:11,215
I'll extend your stay one more night.

741
00:26:11,885 --> 00:26:14,845
(Her true feelings get revealed on her face.)

742
00:26:14,845 --> 00:26:16,485
Jeong Hye, I saw that.

743
00:26:16,915 --> 00:26:18,285
- I saw everything.
- What are you talking about?

744
00:26:18,685 --> 00:26:20,425
I'm happiest when I get to sleep,

745
00:26:20,425 --> 00:26:22,895
hang out, and have dinner with the girls.

746
00:26:22,895 --> 00:26:25,425
- Right?
- How's everything coming along?

747
00:26:25,825 --> 00:26:28,495
I have to keep my eyes on the chestnut cream.

748
00:26:28,495 --> 00:26:30,835
Yes, that one is a baby too.

749
00:26:30,835 --> 00:26:32,835
Gosh, you baby.

750
00:26:33,305 --> 00:26:35,005
(Meanwhile, Mimi is dicing the shrimp.)

751
00:26:35,005 --> 00:26:36,275
I'm done cutting.

752
00:26:36,975 --> 00:26:40,275
If you're done with the shrimp, can you take a look at Yu Jin?

753
00:26:40,275 --> 00:26:41,445
- I'm not done yet.
- Okay.

754
00:26:41,975 --> 00:26:43,175
(She's just done with cutting.)

755
00:26:43,175 --> 00:26:44,615
I'm sorry,

756
00:26:44,915 --> 00:26:46,115
but there's no end to prepping the shrimp.

757
00:26:46,385 --> 00:26:49,285
(She finds Mimi cute, who's powering through a shrimp-patty marathon.)

758
00:26:49,315 --> 00:26:51,315
Is there anything I can help you with?

759
00:26:51,925 --> 00:26:53,555
- Wait.
- Can you help Mi Hyun?

760
00:26:53,555 --> 00:26:55,295
Wait, I'm counting. Give me a second.

761
00:26:55,555 --> 00:26:57,295
(Flustered)

762
00:26:57,295 --> 00:26:58,995
Wait.

763
00:26:59,265 --> 00:27:00,265
I'm done.

764
00:27:00,265 --> 00:27:01,725
- I mean...
- Egg mixture and...

765
00:27:01,725 --> 00:27:03,295
- It's nonsense, isn't it?
- Four?

766
00:27:03,395 --> 00:27:05,935
You should bring a whiteboard here.

767
00:27:05,935 --> 00:27:06,965
I know.

768
00:27:07,465 --> 00:27:08,735
Is this enough?

769
00:27:08,735 --> 00:27:10,575
Yes, that's perfect.

770
00:27:10,975 --> 00:27:11,975
Jeong Hye.

771
00:27:13,245 --> 00:27:14,275
Jeong Hye.

772
00:27:14,605 --> 00:27:16,275
Jeong Hye, why aren't you answering me?

773
00:27:16,475 --> 00:27:18,915
(You're sunshine)

774
00:27:19,015 --> 00:27:21,545
(Responding by singing instead)

775
00:27:21,745 --> 00:27:23,115
(Cheol Yong dances along to Jeong Hye's beautiful voice.)

776
00:27:23,115 --> 00:27:24,455
(Cheol Yong dances along to Jeong Hye's beautiful voice.)

777
00:27:24,485 --> 00:27:27,185
(Perfectly in sync)

778
00:27:27,325 --> 00:27:29,325
If I make a lot of money someday,

779
00:27:29,655 --> 00:27:32,425
will you open a restaurant for me in Seoul?

780
00:27:32,425 --> 00:27:34,625
Of course. How about a rice cake shop?

781
00:27:34,625 --> 00:27:35,665
A rice cake shop sounds lovely.

782
00:27:35,665 --> 00:27:36,935
- Doesn't it?
- Yes.

783
00:27:37,195 --> 00:27:38,665
I'll open a rice cake shop for you.

784
00:27:39,065 --> 00:27:40,335
At our rice cake shop,

785
00:27:40,335 --> 00:27:42,575
you can stir the chestnut cream.

786
00:27:42,835 --> 00:27:44,735
I'll roll out dough with rice cakes.

787
00:27:44,735 --> 00:27:46,245
Wouldn't that be fun?

788
00:27:46,245 --> 00:27:48,675
How can you roll out dough with rice cakes?

789
00:27:48,675 --> 00:27:50,915
Are you saying that we'll make pizza with rice cakes?

790
00:27:50,915 --> 00:27:53,615
With rice cakes, we can make pizza, tiramisu,

791
00:27:53,785 --> 00:27:56,255
lasagna, and pasta!

792
00:27:56,755 --> 00:27:59,155
(Gosh, I get it.)

793
00:27:59,285 --> 00:28:01,625
Jeong Hye, let's live in our own little paradise.

794
00:28:01,685 --> 00:28:02,695
Where would that be?

795
00:28:02,695 --> 00:28:05,895
For me, paradise is tucked under your armpits.

796
00:28:06,095 --> 00:28:08,025
(Then come on in.)

797
00:28:08,025 --> 00:28:10,095
- What's wrong with her?
- Under his armpits?

798
00:28:10,195 --> 00:28:11,235
It's true.

799
00:28:11,235 --> 00:28:13,365
Smelling the scent of the person you love...

800
00:28:13,365 --> 00:28:15,135
makes you all sleepy.

801
00:28:15,505 --> 00:28:17,335
But we haven't even kissed yet.

802
00:28:17,875 --> 00:28:19,145
But we've slept together.

803
00:28:19,645 --> 00:28:20,675
(She means that they stayed at the same accommodation.)

804
00:28:20,675 --> 00:28:21,745
What did you say?

805
00:28:23,215 --> 00:28:24,615
We've slept together.

806
00:28:24,615 --> 00:28:26,115
We just haven't kissed.

807
00:28:26,445 --> 00:28:27,485
You're so cheeky.

808
00:28:27,945 --> 00:28:29,055
She called her cheeky.

809
00:28:29,255 --> 00:28:30,915
I don't like to kiss.

810
00:28:31,155 --> 00:28:32,855
Eun Ji, how's the chestnut cream looking?

811
00:28:32,855 --> 00:28:34,325
I keep stirring it.

812
00:28:34,685 --> 00:28:36,295
You're working hard on that chestnut cream.

813
00:28:37,225 --> 00:28:39,195
If I do this, maybe I'll look better...

814
00:28:39,195 --> 00:28:40,725
at stirring the chestnut cream.

815
00:28:40,925 --> 00:28:43,495
(She got bored of stirring only the chestnut cream.)

816
00:28:44,235 --> 00:28:46,805
(Hide in my arms)

817
00:28:46,805 --> 00:28:49,275
(Without her knowing)

818
00:28:49,335 --> 00:28:51,635
(Bored Eun Ji kicks off a performance.)

819
00:28:51,735 --> 00:28:53,645
(There's a thrill to keeping secrets)

820
00:28:53,745 --> 00:28:54,875
(Just for me)

821
00:28:54,975 --> 00:28:56,075
(Singing)

822
00:28:56,075 --> 00:28:57,075
(You're falling deeper for me)

823
00:28:57,075 --> 00:28:58,845
(They're used to her acting like this.)

824
00:28:58,945 --> 00:29:01,185
(A seductive song)

825
00:29:01,185 --> 00:29:03,615
(Chanting)

826
00:29:03,685 --> 00:29:06,025
- G, g, baby - It reminds me of this.

827
00:29:07,225 --> 00:29:08,725
(Beatboxing)

828
00:29:08,825 --> 00:29:11,725
(Switching genres, she starts deejaying with the stove.)

829
00:29:11,825 --> 00:29:14,125
(Space Rice Cake Nightclub opens.)

830
00:29:14,195 --> 00:29:16,395
(Beatboxing)

831
00:29:16,395 --> 00:29:17,865
(Bang)

832
00:29:17,865 --> 00:29:19,905
(Going all out with beatboxing)

833
00:29:20,435 --> 00:29:22,105
- Bang.
- Gosh, what's going on?

834
00:29:22,435 --> 00:29:23,905
Bang

835
00:29:23,905 --> 00:29:26,045
Eun Ji, how about an exciting song?

836
00:29:26,045 --> 00:29:27,675
(An exciting song?)

837
00:29:29,145 --> 00:29:30,145
Boom

838
00:29:30,145 --> 00:29:31,515
(At Mimi's request, jumping to the highlight)

839
00:29:31,515 --> 00:29:32,545
You're good.

840
00:29:32,745 --> 00:29:34,015
- Is it not enough?
- It's not working.

841
00:29:34,015 --> 00:29:37,585
(Arabian Night)

842
00:29:37,715 --> 00:29:41,885
(This time, she ventures into a musical.)

843
00:29:41,885 --> 00:29:42,895
(The magic lamp)

844
00:29:42,895 --> 00:29:44,055
You must be tired, Jeong Hye.

845
00:29:44,125 --> 00:29:45,925
(Three wishes)

846
00:29:46,025 --> 00:29:48,865
(Lost in the moment)

847
00:29:49,035 --> 00:29:52,805
(Arabian Night)

848
00:29:52,805 --> 00:29:54,235
(Laughing)

849
00:29:56,035 --> 00:29:57,705
(A sudden change of genre)

850
00:29:57,705 --> 00:29:59,105
So Earth Arcaders can run...

851
00:29:59,105 --> 00:30:01,305
- It's a witch's cream.
- Space Rice Cake...

852
00:30:01,905 --> 00:30:05,245
as their punishment.

853
00:30:06,685 --> 00:30:09,315
Add An Yu Jin.

854
00:30:09,755 --> 00:30:11,415
(A standing ovation for a top-tier performance)

855
00:30:11,415 --> 00:30:14,155
Add Lee Young Ji.

856
00:30:15,055 --> 00:30:19,295
And add Kim Mimi.

857
00:30:19,295 --> 00:30:20,665
It's because she's having a hard time.

858
00:30:21,165 --> 00:30:23,395
The Earth Arcaders will work...

859
00:30:23,395 --> 00:30:26,565
at Space Rice Cake like this.

860
00:30:26,905 --> 00:30:28,735
(Laughing triumphantly)

861
00:30:28,735 --> 00:30:32,035
(And they'll keep prepping too.)

862
00:30:32,375 --> 00:30:33,775
Once you finish making those two pieces,

863
00:30:33,775 --> 00:30:35,075
aren't you done with dough?

864
00:30:35,075 --> 00:30:36,145
Yes, 15 pieces.

865
00:30:36,145 --> 00:30:37,615
(Soon, she's done with the prep.)

866
00:30:37,615 --> 00:30:39,345
- I just have to make two more.
- That was quick.

867
00:30:39,515 --> 00:30:40,985
Eun Ji, I'll stir it for a minute.

868
00:30:41,285 --> 00:30:43,055
- Make sure it doesn't stick.
- Okay.

869
00:30:43,155 --> 00:30:45,185
Eun Ji, I shouldn't touch it...

870
00:30:45,185 --> 00:30:46,355
when it gets stuck, right?

871
00:30:46,355 --> 00:30:47,655
Right. Leave it alone.

872
00:30:48,225 --> 00:30:50,225
Earlier, Kyung Soo said...

873
00:30:50,225 --> 00:30:52,325
that you have a knack for cooking.

874
00:30:52,325 --> 00:30:53,425
- Really?
- Yes.

875
00:30:53,525 --> 00:30:54,795
He says that you have what it takes to be a chef.

876
00:30:54,795 --> 00:30:56,235
- Seriously?
- Yes.

877
00:30:56,235 --> 00:30:57,795
He must have felt something from watching you cook.

878
00:30:57,795 --> 00:30:59,435
- Oh, my.
- I mean, that man.

879
00:30:59,905 --> 00:31:02,235
He should feel something else when he looks at me,

880
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:03,335
but that's what he felt?

881
00:31:03,335 --> 00:31:04,935
(What?)

882
00:31:05,005 --> 00:31:07,175
- Mimi, you made a lot of progress.
- Right?

883
00:31:07,405 --> 00:31:08,775
When Young Ji finishes making her last dough,

884
00:31:08,775 --> 00:31:10,415
I can stop stirring it.

885
00:31:10,415 --> 00:31:12,385
- Eun Ji, that looks enough.
- It's enough.

886
00:31:12,585 --> 00:31:13,815
It turned out really well.

887
00:31:13,815 --> 00:31:15,655
Well done, Eun Ji.

888
00:31:17,015 --> 00:31:18,985
Be careful. Nice.

889
00:31:18,985 --> 00:31:21,485
- Well done, everyone.
- Well done.

890
00:31:21,485 --> 00:31:23,195
Good job.

891
00:31:23,355 --> 00:31:25,695
Gosh, I want to be gone with the wind.

892
00:31:25,865 --> 00:31:27,565
Let's go. Let's be gone with the wind.

893
00:31:27,765 --> 00:31:28,935
Let's clean up and go home.

894
00:31:28,935 --> 00:31:29,995
- Let's go.
- Okay, Eun Ji.

895
00:31:29,995 --> 00:31:31,035
All right.

896
00:31:31,395 --> 00:31:32,765
Well done.

897
00:31:33,465 --> 00:31:34,505
Good job.

898
00:31:37,305 --> 00:31:40,175
(The weather is gloomy today.)

899
00:31:40,175 --> 00:31:41,275
It's raining.

900
00:31:42,775 --> 00:31:46,085
Why on the last day of our business?

901
00:31:46,845 --> 00:31:50,055
Is this business cursed or something?

902
00:31:51,285 --> 00:31:52,685
On the first day and the last day...

903
00:31:53,525 --> 00:31:56,655
(Rain or shine, she needs her sugar fix.)

904
00:31:57,155 --> 00:31:58,355
My goodness.

905
00:31:59,165 --> 00:32:00,895
It's so funny to see you eat caramel cookies...

906
00:32:00,895 --> 00:32:02,025
first thing in the morning.

907
00:32:03,665 --> 00:32:04,695
It's delicious.

908
00:32:05,965 --> 00:32:08,305
Seeing you eat makes me hungry.

909
00:32:08,605 --> 00:32:10,135
You should eat.

910
00:32:11,535 --> 00:32:13,445
Yu Jin, it's our last day.

911
00:32:14,045 --> 00:32:15,345
It's completely insane.

912
00:32:15,575 --> 00:32:17,345
It's really insane, Yu Jin.

913
00:32:17,345 --> 00:32:18,415
It's unbelievable.

914
00:32:18,415 --> 00:32:20,545
I can't believe that it's finally our last day.

915
00:32:21,545 --> 00:32:24,155
- It's our last day.
- Yes.

916
00:32:25,015 --> 00:32:27,085
Girls, it's finally our last day.

917
00:32:27,085 --> 00:32:28,525
It's really a bummer.

918
00:32:29,025 --> 00:32:30,595
- Is it a bummer?
- Yes.

919
00:32:31,095 --> 00:32:32,195
I can understand.

920
00:32:33,125 --> 00:32:35,395
(She respects different opinions.)

921
00:32:36,035 --> 00:32:38,265
- Hey, it's raining.
- Yes.

922
00:32:38,265 --> 00:32:39,735
On the first and the last day,

923
00:32:39,835 --> 00:32:42,105
- I know. I said the same thing.
- it's raining.

924
00:32:42,105 --> 00:32:43,905
What do you call it when the same thing happens?

925
00:32:44,135 --> 00:32:45,505
- A cyclic structure?
- Yes.

926
00:32:46,345 --> 00:32:48,975
Young Ji, it's creepy how it's raining like it did...

927
00:32:48,975 --> 00:32:50,015
on our first day.

928
00:32:50,275 --> 00:32:52,045
- Seriously, Eun Ji.
- It's so intriguing.

929
00:32:52,045 --> 00:32:53,385
It's really creepy.

930
00:32:53,415 --> 00:32:55,315
How can the ending be the same as the beginning?

931
00:32:55,685 --> 00:32:57,415
- Can I say one thing?
- Sure.

932
00:32:57,855 --> 00:33:00,125
I bet something huge will happen today.

933
00:33:00,125 --> 00:33:01,455
Don't say that.

934
00:33:03,055 --> 00:33:05,255
Girls, it's already 8:50am. Oh, no.

935
00:33:05,765 --> 00:33:08,665
(Her hands start moving faster.)

936
00:33:09,535 --> 00:33:11,935
Could someone tell me that this is a dream?

937
00:33:13,035 --> 00:33:14,435
I'm really scared.

938
00:33:15,265 --> 00:33:17,005
Are we really running a restaurant today?

939
00:33:17,335 --> 00:33:18,575
Can you just give me ten minutes?

940
00:33:19,475 --> 00:33:21,745
How did time fly by so fast?

941
00:33:22,315 --> 00:33:24,075
Why is there a dishcloth in my bag?

942
00:33:24,915 --> 00:33:26,885
My goodness. Time flew by.

943
00:33:26,885 --> 00:33:29,015
I can't believe it. I'd better pack my battery.

944
00:33:29,485 --> 00:33:30,815
Today, it's a wicked spirit showdown.

945
00:33:30,815 --> 00:33:33,225
I'll take on the dishwashing spirit.

946
00:33:33,525 --> 00:33:35,055
My wicked spirit for today will be...

947
00:33:35,055 --> 00:33:38,525
the need to clean up the second floor.

948
00:33:38,855 --> 00:33:40,095
We need to ask...

949
00:33:40,095 --> 00:33:41,325
- Middle-aged Man for help today.
- Right.

950
00:33:41,325 --> 00:33:42,765
- We have no part-timer today.
- We will need...

951
00:33:42,765 --> 00:33:44,095
Middle-aged Man's help.

952
00:33:45,835 --> 00:33:48,465
Should I hide all the pomegranate in the pantry?

953
00:33:49,075 --> 00:33:51,205
"We can't sell any because we're out of pomegranate."

954
00:33:52,545 --> 00:33:54,545
- What should we do?
- Today is the last day of business.

955
00:33:54,545 --> 00:33:55,615
What do you want to do?

956
00:33:55,975 --> 00:33:57,845
(They're very worried about their last day of business.)

957
00:33:57,845 --> 00:33:58,875
Shall we get going?

958
00:33:59,145 --> 00:34:01,015
Let's go. It's 9:10am.

959
00:34:02,245 --> 00:34:03,885
- It's raining a lot.
- It's raining hard.

960
00:34:03,885 --> 00:34:06,355
- It's the same as the first day.
- What?

961
00:34:07,155 --> 00:34:10,255
We're in trouble. Why is this happening?

962
00:34:10,795 --> 00:34:12,995
Gosh, it's really raining today.

963
00:34:13,195 --> 00:34:15,365
Isn't it unbelievable that it's raining?

964
00:34:15,365 --> 00:34:17,495
What do you mean by the rain on the first day?

965
00:34:17,495 --> 00:34:18,735
Like a full-blown typhoon.

966
00:34:18,735 --> 00:34:21,165
- On the first day of our business?
- Yes.

967
00:34:21,165 --> 00:34:22,575
- Not when Yeong Seok came?
- Right.

968
00:34:22,575 --> 00:34:23,805
Oh, that's right.

969
00:34:23,805 --> 00:34:25,305
- The first day of our business.
- Right.

970
00:34:25,305 --> 00:34:27,105
The windows were open, so rain was pouring right in.

971
00:34:27,105 --> 00:34:29,145
- It was absolute chaos.
- It feels like it's been a year.

972
00:34:29,315 --> 00:34:30,915
It does feel like last year.

973
00:34:31,515 --> 00:34:33,315
- It's unbelievable.
- It's only been a week.

974
00:34:33,315 --> 00:34:35,345
- Exactly.
- I can't believe...

975
00:34:35,345 --> 00:34:36,455
that it really happened.

976
00:34:36,715 --> 00:34:39,285
Today... Let me say one thing.

977
00:34:39,555 --> 00:34:41,385
I won't respect the customers today.

978
00:34:41,755 --> 00:34:42,955
(Let's hear what she has to say.)

979
00:34:42,955 --> 00:34:44,525
- What do you mean?
- Are you saying that out loud?

980
00:34:44,725 --> 00:34:47,025
Even if you serve everything except pomegranate ade,

981
00:34:47,025 --> 00:34:48,565
I'll be okay with it.

982
00:34:49,095 --> 00:34:50,995
We need to prioritize the drinks first.

983
00:34:51,665 --> 00:34:53,935
- We should serve the drinks first.
- Yes.

984
00:34:54,865 --> 00:34:56,275
We have two hours for the prep.

985
00:34:56,275 --> 00:34:58,505
Gosh, what do we do?

986
00:34:58,505 --> 00:35:00,245
(As if things weren't bad enough, there's even heavy traffic.)

987
00:35:00,605 --> 00:35:01,905
We should've slept in the kitchen.

988
00:35:02,475 --> 00:35:03,845
That's nonsense.

989
00:35:04,215 --> 00:35:05,645
With a mat...

990
00:35:05,645 --> 00:35:07,115
- on the kitchen floor?
- Yes.

991
00:35:07,115 --> 00:35:09,585
- That sounds nice.
- It would be fascinating.

992
00:35:10,555 --> 00:35:11,715
Gosh, today...

993
00:35:11,815 --> 00:35:13,055
(Sighing)

994
00:35:13,055 --> 00:35:15,795
Since it's our last day, I want to serve all the dishes.

995
00:35:15,795 --> 00:35:16,795
- Right?
- Right.

996
00:35:16,795 --> 00:35:19,195
Yu Jin, we have to do this as soon as we get there.

997
00:35:19,195 --> 00:35:21,295
We have to make coffee.

998
00:35:21,495 --> 00:35:22,535
I don't want to.

999
00:35:22,535 --> 00:35:24,365
We have to make syrup.

1000
00:35:24,365 --> 00:35:25,395
No way.

1001
00:35:26,205 --> 00:35:27,265
I don't want to.

1002
00:35:28,105 --> 00:35:30,305
- We have to make whipped cream.
- We do?

1003
00:35:30,305 --> 00:35:31,305
- For the mint cream.
- The mint cream.

1004
00:35:31,535 --> 00:35:34,075
Are we selling original tteokbokki and lasagna today?

1005
00:35:34,075 --> 00:35:35,675
No, pollack roe and clam pasta.

1006
00:35:35,675 --> 00:35:37,945
Tteokbokki and pollack roe and clam pasta will revive.

1007
00:35:38,175 --> 00:35:39,315
- My goodness.
- I'll change all the names...

1008
00:35:39,315 --> 00:35:40,415
as soon as we arrive.

1009
00:35:40,685 --> 00:35:41,685
Right, the names.

1010
00:35:41,915 --> 00:35:43,055
We're almost there.

1011
00:35:43,355 --> 00:35:45,255
Oh, my gosh. What do I do?

1012
00:35:45,255 --> 00:35:46,585
Get ready for the prep.

1013
00:35:47,255 --> 00:35:48,925
We can do this.

1014
00:35:48,925 --> 00:35:49,925
Stay strong until the end.

1015
00:35:51,795 --> 00:35:52,895
Just simply park.

1016
00:35:54,195 --> 00:35:55,425
Preparing comes first.

1017
00:35:56,835 --> 00:35:59,205
(The rice cakes from the HQ arrive for the last time.)

1018
00:35:59,605 --> 00:36:01,465
- Mimi, carry them with me.
- Okay.

1019
00:36:02,435 --> 00:36:04,935
- Eun Ji, jeolpyeon is here.
- Good job.

1020
00:36:05,875 --> 00:36:08,175
- The last day. Let's do this.
- Let's go.

1021
00:36:08,345 --> 00:36:09,815
- Yes.
- Let's do this.

1022
00:36:10,275 --> 00:36:12,015
Why did you write "affection" today?

1023
00:36:12,715 --> 00:36:14,945
Because my affection for the shop has grown a lot.

1024
