00:55:08,785 --> 00:55:10,885
It's Chestnut Tyranno.

1523
00:55:10,885 --> 00:55:12,685
Please try it when you're done with the main dish.

1524
00:55:13,115 --> 00:55:14,455
Sorry for being so loud.

1525
00:55:14,455 --> 00:55:15,585
I startled you.

1526
00:55:16,085 --> 00:55:18,025
(Biting)

1527
00:55:19,355 --> 00:55:20,565
- It's good, isn't it?
- Yes, it's good.

1528
00:55:21,565 --> 00:55:24,695
(It's as tasty as its dramatic name.)

1529
00:55:24,695 --> 00:55:25,895
Welcome.

1530
00:55:26,095 --> 00:55:27,105
- Hello.
- Hello.

1531
00:55:27,105 --> 00:55:28,465
Hello. Nice to meet you.

1532
00:55:28,465 --> 00:55:30,375
- You're so cute.
- Thanks.

1533
00:55:30,635 --> 00:55:32,035
Today is our last day,

1534
00:55:32,035 --> 00:55:34,475
- so I couldn't wear full makeup.
- You're so pretty.

1535
00:55:34,475 --> 00:55:36,845
- I couldn't wear proper makeup.
- It's right up my alley.

1536
00:55:36,845 --> 00:55:38,275
- I'll apologize for that.
- Eun Ji,

1537
00:55:38,275 --> 00:55:39,975
I feel like I'm watching a video clip.

1538
00:55:40,415 --> 00:55:42,145
- No, you're so pretty.
- You're so pretty.

1539
00:55:42,145 --> 00:55:43,145
Thank you.

1540
00:55:43,145 --> 00:55:44,385
I'm nervous right now.

1541
00:55:44,385 --> 00:55:45,515
What is your name?

1542
00:55:45,785 --> 00:55:47,555
(No, you're so pretty.)

1543
00:55:47,555 --> 00:55:48,555
(Laughing)

1544
00:55:48,885 --> 00:55:50,455
She's enjoying the moment.

1545
00:55:51,255 --> 00:55:53,495
One Jeolpyeon Ghost Rice Cake Pasta.

1546
00:55:53,495 --> 00:55:55,425
That's the pollack roe pasta, isn't it?

1547
00:55:56,965 --> 00:55:58,095
How did you know?

1548
00:55:58,595 --> 00:56:01,465
It's pollack roe meets Manila clams.

1549
00:56:01,935 --> 00:56:04,835
Plus, it's made by Jeolpyeon Ghost.

1550
00:56:04,835 --> 00:56:06,205
That sounds delicious.

1551
00:56:06,435 --> 00:56:09,075
We recreated it in a shamanic style.

1552
00:56:09,075 --> 00:56:10,575
We added a touch of shamanism.

1553
00:56:10,945 --> 00:56:12,375
I'm so into shamanism.

1554
00:56:12,375 --> 00:56:14,445
- Are you into shamanism?
- Yes, I love it.

1555
00:56:14,445 --> 00:56:16,015
What do you have in abundance in your saju, water or fire?

1556
00:56:16,015 --> 00:56:17,315
- I have lots of trees.
- Trees?

1557
00:56:17,315 --> 00:56:19,055
- We'd get along well.
- My goodness.

1558
00:56:19,055 --> 00:56:20,425
I'm all trees.

1559
00:56:20,425 --> 00:56:22,055
- I lack trees.
- Gosh.

1560
00:56:22,055 --> 00:56:23,855
- I'll recharge your tree element.
- Great.

1561
00:56:23,855 --> 00:56:24,925
Touch me.

1562
00:56:25,255 --> 00:56:26,795
- Charging.
- I'll charge you.

1563
00:56:26,795 --> 00:56:27,965
Does it feel good?

1564
00:56:27,965 --> 00:56:30,295
I'm recharged. Thank you so much.

1565
00:56:30,295 --> 00:56:32,735
Also, we'll get Chestnut Tyranno.

1566
00:56:32,865 --> 00:56:34,365
Chestnut Tyranno!

1567
00:56:35,235 --> 00:56:36,405
Chestnut Tyranno.

1568
00:56:36,405 --> 00:56:37,735
(A fair trade of energy)

1569
00:56:37,735 --> 00:56:38,805
- Good.
- Thanks.

1570
00:56:38,805 --> 00:56:40,975
Your total would be 47.2 dollars.

1571
00:56:40,975 --> 00:56:41,975
Okay.

1572
00:56:41,975 --> 00:56:43,445
- We have an order.
- Okay.

1573
00:56:43,445 --> 00:56:45,575
It's 1 tteokbokki, 1 shrimp burger,

1574
00:56:45,575 --> 00:56:47,915
and 1 Rice Cake Pasta. Also, Chestnut Tyranno...

1575
00:56:48,215 --> 00:56:49,785
- for one person. And ade.
- Okay.

1576
00:56:50,185 --> 00:56:51,415
I'll start the tteokbokki first.

1577
00:56:51,415 --> 00:56:52,615
(Table 6: Lee Young Ji Resurrection Tteokbokki, 1)

1578
00:56:52,785 --> 00:56:55,255
(She puts garaetteok first.)

1579
00:56:55,555 --> 00:56:57,755
(With the chef's rustic touch...)

1580
00:56:57,895 --> 00:57:01,065
Yes, over there. Good job, tteokbokki. Gosh.

1581
00:57:01,365 --> 00:57:02,665
The shrimp burger is ready.

1582
00:57:02,895 --> 00:57:04,265
We'll serve it with the tteokbokki.

1583
00:57:04,265 --> 00:57:06,495
Okay. But I need to do the dishes soon.

1584
00:57:06,795 --> 00:57:08,035
Do you want me to serve them?

1585
00:57:08,135 --> 00:57:09,435
Yes. Please go ahead.

1586
00:57:10,165 --> 00:57:12,075
Gosh. That was fast.

1587
00:57:12,075 --> 00:57:13,335
Good. Fantastic.

1588
00:57:13,505 --> 00:57:15,045
- This is better. You can go first.
- Okay.

1589
00:57:16,075 --> 00:57:20,415
(She heads to the 2nd floor with a tray full of food.)

1590
00:57:20,415 --> 00:57:22,445
- Is this Table Six?
- Hello.

1591
00:57:22,615 --> 00:57:24,255
Hello.

1592
00:57:24,685 --> 00:57:27,025
I just made this one.

1593
00:57:27,125 --> 00:57:29,555
- Goodness.
- Gosh. It looks so good.

1594
00:57:29,555 --> 00:57:31,695
I just made this one also.

1595
00:57:31,695 --> 00:57:32,695
Really?

1596
00:57:33,095 --> 00:57:36,095
I don't usually serve the food because we're busy in the kitchen.

1597
00:57:36,095 --> 00:57:37,795
- Thank you.
- Don't touch this.

1598
00:57:37,795 --> 00:57:38,895
- Right. Okay.
- Okay.

1599
00:57:39,865 --> 00:57:42,035
- They're really tasty. Enjoy.
- Thank you. Okay.

1600
00:57:42,035 --> 00:57:43,205
(Table 6: Jeolpyeon Ghost Rice Cake Pasta, pomegranate ade)

1601
00:57:43,205 --> 00:57:44,235
- Shall we?
- Yes.

1602
00:57:44,535 --> 00:57:45,905
(New customers are entering.)

1603
00:57:46,375 --> 00:57:48,805
Come in. Customers are king at Space Rice Cake.

1604
00:57:49,605 --> 00:57:51,575
It's our last business day.

1605
00:57:51,745 --> 00:57:53,115
I hope you ordered everything you wanted.

1606
00:57:54,385 --> 00:57:56,515
(Unlike her morning resolution, )

1607
00:57:56,515 --> 00:57:59,115
(she's dedicated to customer service.)

1608
00:57:59,455 --> 00:58:02,625
(Next customers arrive through the rain.)

1609
00:58:02,785 --> 00:58:04,025
(Space Rice Cake's youngest customer is here.)

1610
00:58:04,025 --> 00:58:05,425
There's an umbrella stand on the right.

1611
00:58:05,625 --> 00:58:06,925
I think we have customers.

1612
00:58:06,925 --> 00:58:08,125
Hello.

1613
00:58:08,665 --> 00:58:10,795
Hello. Our customers are the king.

1614
00:58:11,895 --> 00:58:14,005
- Hello. Gosh. The baby's asleep.
- Hello.

1615
00:58:14,005 --> 00:58:15,005
(Loud)

1616
00:58:15,235 --> 00:58:17,275
Young Ji. A baby is asleep.

1617
00:58:17,535 --> 00:58:18,635
Sorry.

1618
00:58:19,705 --> 00:58:21,575
Why am I putting myself through this? What for?

1619
00:58:22,275 --> 00:58:24,515
- I can hear you.
- Gosh. Sorry.

1620
00:58:25,115 --> 00:58:27,285
- Is it raining heavily outside?
- Yes.

1621
00:58:28,115 --> 00:58:30,755
- We'll get 1 beef burger.
- Okay. It's 1 beef burger.

1622
00:58:30,755 --> 00:58:32,585
- What about the shrimp one?
- We won't be able to finish it.

1623
00:58:32,585 --> 00:58:34,055
(The baby is fussing.)

1624
00:58:34,225 --> 00:58:35,355
Goodness. Little one.

1625
00:58:35,785 --> 00:58:37,895
Please put this on your table.

1626
00:58:37,895 --> 00:58:39,725
Thank you. Do you need your receipt?

1627
00:58:39,725 --> 00:58:40,795
- No.
- Okay.

1628
00:58:40,965 --> 00:58:42,525
Here's the order.

1629
00:58:42,695 --> 00:58:44,965
It's 1 pomegranate ade, 1 Rice Cake Pasta,

1630
00:58:44,965 --> 00:58:46,095
and 1 beef burger.

1631
00:58:46,495 --> 00:58:47,965
As for the baby customer,

1632
00:58:47,965 --> 00:58:49,865
it's its first day out.

1633
00:58:49,865 --> 00:58:51,205
- Really?
- The baby's just over 100 days old.

1634
00:58:51,205 --> 00:58:53,805
That's why it started crying after hearing such a loud noise.

1635
00:58:53,805 --> 00:58:55,605
It cried like a baby.

1636
00:58:55,775 --> 00:58:58,145
I told you to keep quiet.

1637
00:58:58,875 --> 00:59:00,915
You startled the baby.

1638
00:59:01,515 --> 00:59:04,385
(After hearing the news, Eun Ji visits them with the ade.)

1639
00:59:04,685 --> 00:59:06,915
- Here's your drink.
- Hello.

1640
00:59:06,915 --> 00:59:09,385
- This is the pomegranate ade.
- Thanks.

1641
00:59:09,385 --> 00:59:11,455
That's an adorable photo of your baby.

1642
00:59:11,755 --> 00:59:12,795
Thank you.

1643
00:59:13,125 --> 00:59:15,395
Congratulations on leaving the house after 100 days.

1644
00:59:15,825 --> 00:59:17,695
I heard the baby cried a lot...

1645
00:59:17,695 --> 00:59:19,735
- because of our head chef.
- Right.

1646
00:59:20,065 --> 00:59:21,705
- My sincere apologies.
- Thanks.

1647
00:59:21,935 --> 00:59:23,205
The two of you...

1648
00:59:23,205 --> 00:59:25,075
- did a wonderful job.
- Thank you.

1649
00:59:25,075 --> 00:59:27,475
To celebrate your baby's 100th day...

1650
00:59:28,005 --> 00:59:29,445
(Approaching)

1651
00:59:30,245 --> 00:59:32,445
(For 100 days)

1652
00:59:34,645 --> 00:59:36,985
(The baby's first entertainment is Eun Ji's performance.)

1653
00:59:36,985 --> 00:59:38,155
Gosh. This is an expensive performance.

1654
00:59:38,355 --> 00:59:40,415
(Staring)

1655
00:59:41,055 --> 00:59:46,895
(You went through a lot over the past 100 days)

1656
00:59:47,625 --> 00:59:48,795
(It's a performance for the baby...)

1657
00:59:48,795 --> 00:59:49,965
(who did its best to grow up over the past 100 days.)

1658
00:59:49,965 --> 00:59:50,965
Congratulations.

1659
00:59:50,965 --> 00:59:52,165
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1660
00:59:52,565 --> 00:59:55,205
- I recited it quietly.
- Yes. Thanks.

1661
00:59:55,205 --> 00:59:57,605
(Thank you.)

1662
00:59:58,075 --> 00:59:59,205
Just for the moment.

1663
00:59:59,205 --> 01:00:02,175
(Meanwhile, Young Ji is...)

1664
01:00:02,445 --> 01:00:04,675
The shrimp burger will be ready after Yu Jin finishes it up.

1665
01:00:06,245 --> 01:00:07,345
Let's see.

1666
01:00:07,345 --> 01:00:08,815
(She goes on to make a beef burger.)

1667
01:00:08,815 --> 01:00:09,945
Good.

1668
01:00:12,955 --> 01:00:13,955
This is...

1669
01:00:13,955 --> 01:00:15,355
(Wide and flat)

1670
01:00:15,685 --> 01:00:17,395
I'm sorry, but is that bindaetteok?

1671
01:00:17,595 --> 01:00:19,495
- What do you mean?
- Why is it so big today?

1672
01:00:19,495 --> 01:00:20,595
(Today, yesterday, It's just spread out.)

1673
01:00:20,665 --> 01:00:22,895
Look at the letter on my forehead.

1674
01:00:23,225 --> 01:00:24,265
"Affection."

1675
01:00:24,265 --> 01:00:25,895
Please slice the bun for me, Mimi.

1676
01:00:26,095 --> 01:00:28,565
That's why we can't make profits.

1677
01:00:28,865 --> 01:00:30,005
- Yu Jin.
- Yes?

1678
01:00:30,005 --> 01:00:31,675
Does it look like bindaetteok?

1679
01:00:32,175 --> 01:00:34,375
It does look a little like bindaetteok.

1680
01:00:34,375 --> 01:00:35,545
The bigger, the better, isn't it?

1681
01:00:36,205 --> 01:00:37,345
I'm sensitive about this.

1682
01:00:37,345 --> 01:00:38,775
(The reason the head chef is so sensitive...)

1683
01:00:38,775 --> 01:00:40,115
I'm super afraid of it.

1684
01:00:40,545 --> 01:00:44,985
(is because the beef patty wasn't fully cooked before.)

1685
01:00:45,315 --> 01:00:46,915
It won't be cooked unless I spread it out.

1686
01:00:46,915 --> 01:00:48,025
(That's why she created the bindaetteok.)

1687
01:00:48,125 --> 01:00:50,625
Come on. Aren't you going to think about our sales?

1688
01:00:50,625 --> 01:00:52,555
Come on. What about our sales?

1689
01:00:52,555 --> 01:00:54,465
- What do you think?
- I'm about to sell my house.

1690
01:00:54,465 --> 01:00:55,525
About what?

1691
01:00:55,725 --> 01:00:57,465
- The head chef keeps...
- Yes.

1692
01:00:58,065 --> 01:00:59,195
giving so much.

1693
01:00:59,195 --> 01:01:00,705
- Does she keep growing so much?
- No.

1694
01:01:01,535 --> 01:01:03,305
She's way too generous with the portions.

1695
01:01:03,305 --> 01:01:04,635
We won't be able to turn a profit.

1696
01:01:04,635 --> 01:01:06,735
I'm a bit scared it'll actually turn out that way.

1697
01:01:08,675 --> 01:01:11,315
(I want to cry too.)

1698
01:01:11,445 --> 01:01:14,285
Gosh. It's sticking out, Head Chef.

1699
01:01:15,215 --> 01:01:16,815
(Sticking out)

1700
01:01:18,485 --> 01:01:20,355
(Confining it)

1701
01:01:20,585 --> 01:01:21,885
Thank you.

1702
01:01:21,885 --> 01:01:23,125
(She puts well-cooked bindaetteok... No, the beef patty.)

1703
01:01:23,685 --> 01:01:25,255
It really is bindaetteok. What do I do?

1704
01:01:26,695 --> 01:01:29,395
(In the kitchen where a new dish is added to the menu every day, )

1705
01:01:31,895 --> 01:01:34,965
(we have a bindaetteok burger now.)

1706
01:01:35,265 --> 01:01:36,935
Too much in a burger

1707
01:01:37,275 --> 01:01:39,275
I thought we got a new order. You surprised me.

1708
01:01:40,005 --> 01:01:42,275
- I was just singing.
- I'll remove this, Mimi.

1709
01:01:42,975 --> 01:01:45,875
They don't order the pizza.

1710
01:01:46,315 --> 01:01:49,345
So I have nothing to do.

1711
01:01:49,985 --> 01:01:52,815
You can go in now.

1712
01:01:52,815 --> 01:01:54,385
(Yu Jin, who has nothing to do, fries some tater tots.)

1713
01:01:54,785 --> 01:01:58,425
(Next, she tries slicing open the rice cake bun.)

1714
01:02:01,725 --> 01:02:03,465
- She's frying the tater tots.
- Goodness.

1715
01:02:03,465 --> 01:02:04,465
Gosh.

1716
01:02:04,465 --> 01:02:06,095
(Goodness.)

1717
01:02:06,365 --> 01:02:07,565
I'll reveal it like this.

1718
01:02:08,835 --> 01:02:10,365
The temperature is too high.

1719
01:02:10,365 --> 01:02:11,375
It's a pass.

1720
01:02:11,475 --> 01:02:13,705
- Hey. Goodness.
- Yu Jin sliced it open.

1721
01:02:13,875 --> 01:02:15,045
We have an order.

1722
01:02:15,475 --> 01:02:17,205
For Table 9, 1 tteokbokki.

1723
01:02:17,205 --> 01:02:18,975
Also, 1 pizza and 1 shrimp burger.

1724
01:02:19,145 --> 01:02:21,585
- And also an ade.
- They ordered a pizza.

1725
01:02:22,085 --> 01:02:23,785
- Do you want me to pour it?
- Yes. Thank you.

1726
01:02:23,785 --> 01:02:25,155
(Yu Jin goes to do her work.)

1727
01:02:25,355 --> 01:02:27,755
(Young Ji does what she needs to do too.)

1728
01:02:30,485 --> 01:02:32,595
(But a piece of shrimp left without saying goodbye.)

1729
01:02:33,455 --> 01:02:35,295
- Mimi.
- Yes?

1730
01:02:35,625 --> 01:02:36,765
It's nothing.

1731
01:02:37,435 --> 01:02:39,935
(She fills the empty spot with the new piece of shrimp.)

1732
01:02:40,165 --> 01:02:41,565
There's one under there.

1733
01:02:41,735 --> 01:02:42,935
- Did it go in?
- Yes.

1734
01:02:43,365 --> 01:02:45,505
It's a secret between us. Mimi will get upset.

1735
01:02:46,135 --> 01:02:49,705
(Fortunately, Mimi's busy.)

1736
01:02:50,075 --> 01:02:52,115
(She's making 2 servings at once!)

1737
01:02:52,115 --> 01:02:54,085
- It's for two tables.
- I know. That's crazy.

1738
01:02:54,285 --> 01:02:56,485
- Totally.
- Because we did tteok-makase,

1739
01:02:56,645 --> 01:02:58,085
you can handle more servings at once.

1740
01:02:58,355 --> 01:03:00,655
True. I can handle a larger quantity.

1741
01:03:01,625 --> 01:03:04,725
The Rice Cake Pasta will be ready soon.

1742
01:03:05,525 --> 01:03:07,625
Here's the tteokbokki.

1743
01:03:07,625 --> 01:03:09,625
(They finish each dish with their skills much improved.)

1744
01:03:09,625 --> 01:03:12,795
Here are two servings of pollack roe and clam pasta.

1745
01:03:13,335 --> 01:03:14,835
The four of you are working...

1746
01:03:14,835 --> 01:03:17,235
more smoothly when there are more dishes on the menu.

1747
01:03:17,805 --> 01:03:20,075
Do you know what makes it work?

1748
01:03:20,075 --> 01:03:21,575
- What is it?
- Experience.

1749
01:03:21,575 --> 01:03:22,775
Is it because you're more experienced?

1750
01:03:23,145 --> 01:03:25,175
- Guess what kind of experience.
- What is it?

1751
01:03:25,175 --> 01:03:27,815
The experience in pretending we're cool when we're going crazy.

1752
01:03:29,485 --> 01:03:31,715
(For example, )

1753
01:03:32,085 --> 01:03:35,185
(there's this one.)

1754
01:03:35,685 --> 01:03:39,255
(Laughing)

1755
01:03:39,555 --> 01:03:41,195
(Her experience came in handy...)

1756
01:03:41,195 --> 01:03:42,965
(when there was a traffic jam of the dishes.)

1757
01:03:43,295 --> 01:03:45,835
(In the end, )

1758
01:03:46,065 --> 01:03:49,465
(she leveled up by tattooing herself.)

1759
01:03:49,665 --> 01:03:51,535
(The day before...)

1760
01:03:52,175 --> 01:03:56,675
(While so many new dishes were created every day, )

1761
01:03:57,145 --> 01:04:00,475
(she had to climb up the Everest of stairs.)

1762
01:04:00,915 --> 01:04:02,715
(She even took care...)

1763
01:04:02,715 --> 01:04:04,485
(of the customers and the Earth Arcaders.)

1764
01:04:04,715 --> 01:04:06,715
(With the experience she earned, )

1765
01:04:06,715 --> 01:04:12,195
(she did her job professionally without a mistake.)

1766
01:04:12,525 --> 01:04:14,825
(All dishes are served!)

1767
01:04:15,265 --> 01:04:18,795
(They clean up the hall after serving the dishes...)

1768
01:04:18,795 --> 01:04:20,765
(without a moment to rest.)

1769
01:04:21,005 --> 01:04:22,735
Yu Jin, should I call the Middle-aged Man?

1770
01:04:23,265 --> 01:04:25,405
I think we'll need them

1771
01:04:25,405 --> 01:04:27,005
- To clean upstairs.
- Yes.

1772
01:04:27,405 --> 01:04:30,305
Please come upstairs and clean up with us, Middle-aged Man.

1773
01:04:31,145 --> 01:04:36,345
(The Middle-aged Man goes wherever people need him.)

1774
01:04:36,785 --> 01:04:39,815
(While the part-timer cleans the hall...)

1775
01:04:40,085 --> 01:04:41,685
I'll get your orders.

1776
01:04:41,685 --> 01:04:42,785
What's your name?

1777
01:04:42,925 --> 01:04:43,955
Here's the order.

1778
01:04:44,395 --> 01:04:48,725
It's 1 Chestnut Tyranno, 1 ade, 1 pizza, 1 tteokbokki,

1779
01:04:48,725 --> 01:04:50,465
- and one beef burger.
- Okay.

1780
01:04:50,865 --> 01:04:53,035
(The head chef washes her hands again.)

1781
01:04:53,265 --> 01:04:54,335
This is good enough, right?

1782
01:04:54,965 --> 01:04:56,005
Yes.

1783
01:04:56,005 --> 01:04:59,635
(She prepares the tater tots with ease.)

1784
01:05:01,575 --> 01:05:03,345
We've really become masters.

1785
01:05:03,345 --> 01:05:04,475
Gosh. Mimi.

1786
01:05:04,475 --> 01:05:06,215
- That was exactly three minutes.
- Exactly.

1787
01:05:07,545 --> 01:05:09,685
- You're on top of it, Young Ji.
- Did you see that?

1788
01:05:10,985 --> 01:05:13,685
Mimi, the pollack roe... The minced garlic is simmering.

1789
01:05:13,685 --> 01:05:15,455
Thanks for telling me.

1790
01:05:16,185 --> 01:05:17,255
Do you need my help?

1791
01:05:18,995 --> 01:05:21,325
- Stir-fry the pollack roe.
- What?

1792
01:05:21,325 --> 01:05:23,365
That... No, never mind.

1793
01:05:23,365 --> 01:05:24,635
I can do it.

1794
01:05:24,895 --> 01:05:26,865
I'm coming. It's okay.

1795
01:05:27,195 --> 01:05:30,365
Honestly, I can't cook.

1796
01:05:31,405 --> 01:05:32,405
I'm afraid I'll mess it up.

1797
01:05:33,005 --> 01:05:34,035
Same here.

1798
01:05:34,405 --> 01:05:35,905
I can't touch yours either.

1799
01:05:38,575 --> 01:05:40,345
- Lady.
- Yes?

1800
01:05:41,415 --> 01:05:42,415
Why did you call me?

1801
01:05:42,515 --> 01:05:44,815
Lady. After using the crocodile mitt,

1802
01:05:44,815 --> 01:05:46,885
- Sorry.
- should you return it or not?

1803
01:05:47,215 --> 01:05:49,125
(A moment ago)

1804
01:05:49,125 --> 01:05:50,455
I'll borrow your mitt.

1805
01:05:51,795 --> 01:05:53,595
(The crocodile mitt that left the head chef's side...)

1806
01:05:53,595 --> 01:05:54,965
Please understand me.

1807
01:05:56,195 --> 01:05:59,365
(was forced to relocate.)

1808
01:05:59,735 --> 01:06:02,605
I'm sorry. I'll bring it back.

1809
01:06:02,605 --> 01:06:05,475
Bring it back right now. I don't want a mismatched pair.

1810
01:06:05,475 --> 01:06:08,005
- I'll bring it back.
- Bring it back at once.

1811
01:06:08,475 --> 01:06:11,675
I'm sorry. It's so busy upstairs. You don't understand.

1812
01:06:11,675 --> 01:06:13,475
I'm sorry. It's busy, isn't it?

1813
01:06:15,315 --> 01:06:18,085
Hold on. Aren't you giving too many tater tots?

1814
01:06:18,085 --> 01:06:19,455
- Is this okay?
- Why?

1815
01:06:19,455 --> 01:06:21,085
- Is this okay?
- Well.

1816
01:06:21,085 --> 01:06:23,385
- Is it too much?
- We're losing money here.

1817
01:06:23,385 --> 01:06:26,725
It's about affection today. We've grown attached.

1818
01:06:26,825 --> 01:06:28,295
That's why you've been frying tater tots...

1819
01:06:28,295 --> 01:06:29,765
- all day long.
- The beef burger's ready.

1820
01:06:30,595 --> 01:06:31,965
Gosh. She's nagging.

1821
01:06:32,535 --> 01:06:33,635
The beef burger is ready.

1822
01:06:33,865 --> 01:06:35,065
I'm working right now!

1823
01:06:35,305 --> 01:06:38,305
- I still love you.
- I still love you.

1824
01:06:38,475 --> 01:06:40,175
I love you

1825
01:06:40,575 --> 01:06:42,705
I love you so much

1826
01:06:42,705 --> 01:06:44,105
I love you even more.

1827
01:06:44,375 --> 01:06:45,775
- Jeong Hye.
- Yes?

1828
01:06:46,075 --> 01:06:48,085
The time has come.

1829
01:06:48,185 --> 01:06:50,845
We're finally making out today!

1830
01:06:51,415 --> 01:06:53,115
(Laughing)

1831
01:06:53,355 --> 01:06:56,785
I promised Jeong Hye she wouldn't have to work at all.

1832
01:06:57,055 --> 01:06:59,225
You're a liar. Really.

1833
01:06:59,655 --> 01:07:00,995
What can I do?

1834
01:07:01,465 --> 01:07:02,995
Sorry that I'm a loser.

1835
01:07:03,365 --> 01:07:04,395
(Laughing)

1836
01:07:04,495 --> 01:07:05,835
- Yu Jin.
- Yes?

1837
01:07:05,835 --> 01:07:08,335
Is this too much rosemary?

1838
01:07:08,635 --> 01:07:09,665
(Laughing)

1839
01:07:09,665 --> 01:07:12,205
- Is this too hard?
- No, is this rosemary too big?

1840
01:07:12,205 --> 01:07:14,505
That's too big. That's bamboo.

1841
01:07:16,305 --> 01:07:18,375
We've finished five drinks. That's crazy.

1842
01:07:18,815 --> 01:07:20,945
There are only about five tables left.

1843
01:07:20,945 --> 01:07:22,985
- Gosh. Mimi.
- Yes?

1844
01:07:22,985 --> 01:07:24,215
We don't have many tables left.

1845
01:07:24,885 --> 01:07:27,115
- I'm sad for some reason.
- No.

1846
01:07:27,685 --> 01:07:29,625
We want 100 more customers. I'm kidding.

1847
01:07:30,385 --> 01:07:31,725
(Confused)

1848
01:07:31,725 --> 01:07:34,665
- I don't know how I really feel.
- You're afraid it'll come true.

1849
01:07:34,965 --> 01:07:36,395
I don't know how I really feel.

1850
01:07:36,565 --> 01:07:39,965
They should really come. I'm super relaxed today.

1851
01:07:41,105 --> 01:07:42,135
I still love you.

1852
01:07:42,135 --> 01:07:43,205
(Jeong Hye goes serving while they have mixed feelings.)

1853
01:07:43,205 --> 01:07:45,205
- I love you - I'll try to love you.

1854
01:07:45,205 --> 01:07:46,235
I love you

1855
01:07:46,575 --> 01:07:49,605
It seems you're on top of everything.

1856
01:07:49,705 --> 01:07:51,345
As I mentioned before,

1857
01:07:51,345 --> 01:07:53,075
you might end up in red.

1858
01:07:53,275 --> 01:07:55,745
- You need a part-timer?
- No, that's not it.

1859
01:07:56,285 --> 01:07:58,485
I'll double the sales.

1860
01:07:58,485 --> 01:08:00,885
Why don't you accept walk-ins?

1861
01:08:01,785 --> 01:08:03,425
What do you mean?

1862
01:08:03,425 --> 01:08:04,795
- Do we say, "Come in right now?"
- We'll take anyone who comes in.

1863
01:08:04,795 --> 01:08:06,295
- You'll take anyone.
- Let's go.

1864
01:08:06,695 --> 01:08:07,765
- Let's go.
- We'll double the money.

1865
01:08:07,865 --> 01:08:10,465
(Singing)

1866
01:08:10,565 --> 01:08:11,565
More should come.

1867
01:08:11,565 --> 01:08:12,635
(With losses looming, they propose to double the sales count.)

1868
01:08:12,635 --> 01:08:15,065
I've worked my fingers to the bone for a week,

1869
01:08:15,065 --> 01:08:16,405
and you'll double the sales.

1870
01:08:16,405 --> 01:08:18,505
- Is this a rhythm or what?
- But you have to...

1871
01:08:18,505 --> 01:08:19,905
- Exactly.
- It sounds good.

1872
01:08:20,075 --> 01:08:22,205
- Hold on.
- Once the head chef makes the call,

1873
01:08:22,205 --> 01:08:23,575
- we'll open the doors.
- Young Ji.

1874
01:08:23,945 --> 01:08:27,115
- I mean, stop hiding us.
- It's intriguing.

1875
01:08:27,115 --> 01:08:28,415
We have so much dough left, and we need to sell it.

1876
01:08:28,645 --> 01:08:30,785
Look at the leftover pizza dough. It's a shame. What now?

1877
01:08:30,885 --> 01:08:31,885
Hold on.

1878
01:08:32,185 --> 01:08:34,785
(She's torn between two choices as it's become a reality.)

1879
01:08:35,225 --> 01:08:37,355
Do you want an energy drink, Young Ji?

1880
01:08:38,555 --> 01:08:41,525
I can get you an energy drink. Drink it and cheer up.

1881
01:08:41,625 --> 01:08:42,895
Okay. Hold on. I'm coming.

1882
01:08:43,165 --> 01:08:45,035
- Come in.
- I'll join you. It looks fun.

1883
01:08:45,035 --> 01:08:46,165
(So it begins.)

1884
01:08:46,165 --> 01:08:47,195
I want to do it too.

1885
01:08:47,595 --> 01:08:49,265
Let's go.

1886
01:08:49,905 --> 01:08:51,335
(Space Rice Cake)

1887
01:08:51,335 --> 01:08:53,705
Everyone out there, come in!

1888
01:08:53,975 --> 01:08:56,545
We sell tteokbokki!

1889
01:08:56,705 --> 01:08:58,515
There's no line,

1890
01:08:58,515 --> 01:08:59,915
- just come in.
- There's no wait.

1891
01:08:59,915 --> 01:09:02,585
Come in!

1892
01:09:02,585 --> 01:09:04,015
(But...)

1893
01:09:04,115 --> 01:09:05,585
(Space Rice Cake)

1894
01:09:05,585 --> 01:09:07,955
Everyone out there, come in!

1895
01:09:08,355 --> 01:09:10,785
We sell tteokbokki!

1896
01:09:11,125 --> 01:09:12,795
There's no line,

1897
01:09:12,795 --> 01:09:14,195
- just come in.
- There's no wait.

1898
01:09:14,195 --> 01:09:16,665
Come in!

1899
01:09:16,665 --> 01:09:17,735
(But...)

1900
01:09:18,095 --> 01:09:20,235
(there's something they've underestimated.)

1901
01:09:21,365 --> 01:09:23,165
(Raining)

1902
01:09:24,335 --> 01:09:26,535
(Blowing)

1903
01:09:26,875 --> 01:09:29,605
(It's the perfect day...)

1904
01:09:29,605 --> 01:09:31,675
(to stay at home.)

1905
01:09:31,845 --> 01:09:33,415
There's no line.

1906
01:09:33,415 --> 01:09:35,385
(There are only two giant rabbits...)

1907
01:09:35,385 --> 01:09:37,345
(out on the streets in this nasty weather.)

1908
01:09:38,015 --> 01:09:40,385
(We've played this game... We've done this business before.)

1909
01:09:41,055 --> 01:09:48,765
(A bookend: The beginning and the end are connected.)

1910
01:09:49,465 --> 01:09:51,865
- It's raining like our first day.
- What a bookend.

1911
01:09:51,865 --> 01:09:52,935
(They ambitiously take walk-ins, but will customers come?)

1912
01:09:52,935 --> 01:09:53,965
It's legendary.

1913
01:09:53,965 --> 01:09:55,505
(They start taking walk-ins.)

1914
01:09:55,705 --> 01:09:58,505
(They'll double the sales count for the walk-ins.)

1915
01:09:58,775 --> 01:10:00,675
Just for an hour until 2:30pm.

1916
01:10:01,005 --> 01:10:02,475
Start Instagram live, Young Ji.

1917
01:10:04,345 --> 01:10:05,715
What on earth...

1918
01:10:06,445 --> 01:10:08,185
What on earth is going on?

1919
01:10:08,185 --> 01:10:09,645
- Bye.
- Bye.

1920
01:10:09,645 --> 01:10:14,315
(She sends off the customers who are leaving.)

1921
01:10:15,725 --> 01:10:18,755
Hello. Come and have some tteokbokki!

1922
01:10:19,825 --> 01:10:23,125
(After all that decision-making, the streets are practically empty.)

1923
01:10:23,365 --> 01:10:26,395
Yes. Hello. The baby's asleep. I'm sorry.

1924
01:10:26,735 --> 01:10:28,265
Take this one too, Boss.

1925
01:10:28,765 --> 01:10:29,805
I'm busy.

1926
01:10:30,005 --> 01:10:31,575
- I'll go with you.
- Okay.

1927
01:10:32,505 --> 01:10:34,205
- Did you order a beef burger?
- Yes.

1928
01:10:34,205 --> 01:10:35,575
(Since there are no walk-ins, she serves the food herself.)

1929
01:10:35,575 --> 01:10:37,305
- Thank you.
- Please enjoy.

1930
01:10:37,305 --> 01:10:38,345
(Since there are no walk-ins, she serves the food herself.)

1931
01:10:38,515 --> 01:10:40,115
- Do you like it?
- We love it.

1932
01:10:40,115 --> 01:10:41,185
It's me.

1933
01:10:41,985 --> 01:10:43,415
(She's not good at getting people to come in, )

1934
01:10:43,415 --> 01:10:44,815
(but she's a good cook.)

1935
01:10:45,955 --> 01:10:48,085
(Outside, in the meantime, )

1936
01:10:48,525 --> 01:10:51,695
(the customers they've been waiting for are coming.)

1937
01:10:54,865 --> 01:10:56,665
Hello.

1938
01:10:57,425 --> 01:10:59,135
- Did you reserve on CatchTable?
- Yes.

1939
01:10:59,135 --> 01:11:01,735
The ladies who take orders...

1940
01:11:01,865 --> 01:11:04,235
are upstairs right now.

1941
01:11:04,365 --> 01:11:05,405
We have customers.

1942
01:11:05,775 --> 01:11:08,105
- Welcome.
- Please take a look around.

1943
01:11:08,475 --> 01:11:09,975
Lee Ha Yeon.

1944
01:11:09,975 --> 01:11:11,445
(She takes over and takes the order.)

1945
01:11:14,015 --> 01:11:16,415
(A woman still dreaming of striking it rich)

1946
01:11:16,745 --> 01:11:18,785
(The streets are still empty.)

1947
01:11:21,385 --> 01:11:23,985
Hello. Have you eaten?

1948
01:11:23,985 --> 01:11:24,995
(A car stops in front of her.)

1949
01:11:25,255 --> 01:11:27,155
Do you want to eat here?

1950
01:11:28,225 --> 01:11:30,125
You can come in right now.

1951
01:11:30,625 --> 01:11:32,335
Why is she so enthusiastic?

1952
01:11:32,565 --> 01:11:34,365
Why is she attracting customers so pro-actively?

1953
01:11:35,505 --> 01:11:36,735
Do you want to come?

1954
01:11:37,335 --> 01:11:38,535
Come.

1955
01:11:38,535 --> 01:11:40,435
(Since the first day in Goheung, she's never been this passionate.)

1956
01:11:40,635 --> 01:11:44,205
I attracted a couple of customers. They're coming.

1957
01:11:44,205 --> 01:11:46,215
- Good job, Mimi.
- Yes.

1958
01:11:46,745 --> 01:11:48,885
That's twice as much. We're counting each sale double.

1959
01:11:49,545 --> 01:11:51,185
We have to hurry. We have to make it happen.

1960
01:11:51,785 --> 01:11:52,855
I don't know.

1961
01:11:54,015 --> 01:11:55,925
- Do you need the receipt?
- No, it's okay.

1962
01:11:55,925 --> 01:11:56,985
Okay.

1963
01:11:56,985 --> 01:11:59,625
A pomegranate ade, a yuzu ade, a mint cake,

1964
01:11:59,625 --> 01:12:01,825
a Chestnut Tyranno, a Rice Cake Pasta, a pizza,

1965
01:12:01,825 --> 01:12:04,195
a shrimp burger, a beef burger, and a tteokbokki.

1966
01:12:04,425 --> 01:12:06,765
(It would've been great if the orders were from a walk-in.)

1967
01:12:07,295 --> 01:12:08,365
So,

1968
01:12:08,965 --> 01:12:11,105
Confucius and Laozi said,

1969
01:12:12,175 --> 01:12:14,375
"You'll get closer to it once you let it go."

1970
01:12:15,875 --> 01:12:17,405
We let go of everything.

1971
01:12:17,745 --> 01:12:20,615
- Not even an ant is passing by.
- Really?

1972
01:12:21,175 --> 01:12:23,615
- Not a soul in sight.
- Let me take a look.

1973
01:12:23,915 --> 01:12:27,285
(At that moment, rain-soaked ants, or the customers, are coming in.)

1974
01:12:27,555 --> 01:12:28,755
You're here.

1975
01:12:29,325 --> 01:12:31,395
- Were you on the other side?
- No.

1976
01:12:31,595 --> 01:12:33,625
No? Did you make a reservation on CatchTable?

1977
01:12:33,625 --> 01:12:34,795
- No. We're walk-ins.
- We're walk-ins.

1978
01:12:34,795 --> 01:12:36,495
You just came spontaneously. Come in.

1979
01:12:36,765 --> 01:12:39,095
(The first walk-in customers are arriving.)

1980
01:12:39,665 --> 01:12:41,305
We have a team of walk-ins.

1981
01:12:41,305 --> 01:12:42,335
(Bragging it to the HQ)

1982
01:12:42,535 --> 01:12:43,535
(Yu Jin takes their order.)

1983
01:12:43,535 --> 01:12:45,035
Hello.

1984
01:12:45,975 --> 01:12:47,705
The customers are rushing in now, Mimi.

1985
01:12:48,645 --> 01:12:50,005
I asked lots of people to come.

1986
01:12:50,975 --> 01:12:52,415
They love the pollack roe pasta.

1987
01:12:53,215 --> 01:12:54,815
- Do we have more pollack roe?
- Yes.

1988
01:12:54,815 --> 01:12:57,545
- We're out of cuttlefish.
- I just grilled more of them.

1989
01:12:57,545 --> 01:12:58,915
They like the pollack roe pasta.

1990
01:12:58,915 --> 01:13:00,855
Do they like it? Thank you.

1991
01:13:01,485 --> 01:13:04,185
Rice Cake Pasta, pizza, and beef. One of each, right?

1992
01:13:04,185 --> 01:13:06,625
- And we'll get desserts.
- We'll get two desserts.

1993
01:13:07,055 --> 01:13:09,865
(She comes into the kitchen with the order sheet.)

1994
01:13:10,095 --> 01:13:11,695
I'll take the tteokbokki.

1995
01:13:11,965 --> 01:13:13,295
- It's for Table Two.
- Okay.

1996
01:13:13,295 --> 01:13:14,665
(After talking to Eun Ji...)

1997
01:13:14,865 --> 01:13:15,935
Where did it all go?

1998
01:13:16,705 --> 01:13:19,275
(and looking for the pen she lost, )

1999
01:13:20,275 --> 01:13:21,275
(she marks the order sheet...)

2000
01:13:21,275 --> 01:13:22,375
I'll get more cuttlefish.

2001
01:13:22,375 --> 01:13:23,375
(and forgets to call out the order.)

2002
01:13:23,705 --> 01:13:25,315
(However, )

2003
01:13:25,315 --> 01:13:26,375
- Where?
- I'll get more cuttlefish.

2004
01:13:26,375 --> 01:13:28,545
(hiding in the order sheet she scratched out...)

2005
01:13:29,145 --> 01:13:31,985
(was a Chestnut Tyranno.)

2006
01:13:32,455 --> 01:13:34,115
(Unaware of this, )

2007
01:13:34,315 --> 01:13:35,385
(Yu Jin discards the order sheet.)

2008
01:13:35,385 --> 01:13:36,525
I'll be back.

2009
01:13:37,585 --> 01:13:38,925
Table Two is done. Awesome.

2010
01:13:39,725 --> 01:13:40,925
(Eun Ji heads out to serve with the wrong information.)

2011
01:13:40,925 --> 01:13:42,465
Thank you.

2012
01:13:43,565 --> 01:13:44,965
Here's your tteokbokki.

2013
01:13:44,965 --> 01:13:47,895
(Table 2: Chestnut Tyranno, omitted)

2014
01:13:48,535 --> 01:13:50,105
(The customers are enjoying the food without realizing it.)

2015
01:13:50,105 --> 01:13:51,235
The tteokbokki is delicious.

2016
01:13:51,775 --> 01:13:53,035
This tastes better.

2017
01:13:55,245 --> 01:13:56,605
(Meanwhile, Yu Jin)

2018
01:13:56,605 --> 01:14:00,075
- There are two pizzas.
- Two pizzas? Let's go.

2019
01:14:00,075 --> 01:14:01,315
(She gets ready to make pizza.)

2020
01:14:01,515 --> 01:14:04,855
Can I try making 2 pizzas on 1 tray?

2021
01:14:05,115 --> 01:14:07,155
Yes, that sounds good.

2022
01:14:07,485 --> 01:14:08,855
Won't it be very efficient?

2023
01:14:09,185 --> 01:14:10,755
Totally.

2024
01:14:10,885 --> 01:14:13,325
- It'll be super efficient.
- Definitely.

2025
01:14:14,125 --> 01:14:15,465
Gosh, hello.

2026
01:14:15,465 --> 01:14:16,465
I took a photo of this.

2027
01:14:16,465 --> 01:14:18,635
- The menu.
- Okay. Take care.

2028
01:14:18,635 --> 01:14:21,065
- Goodbye.
- Thank you for the food.

2029
01:14:21,335 --> 01:14:23,005
I said "super efficient,"

2030
01:14:23,005 --> 01:14:24,305
and they must've heard it.

2031
01:14:24,305 --> 01:14:26,105
It's okay. This is "Earth Arcade."

2032
01:14:26,305 --> 01:14:27,775
I'm so embarrassed.

2033
01:14:28,445 --> 01:14:29,575
Stay strong.

2034
01:14:30,245 --> 01:14:31,815
Why are you cheering for me when I feel embarrassed?

2035
01:14:32,445 --> 01:14:34,785
We've been putting on pain patches...

2036
01:14:34,785 --> 01:14:35,885
Hello.

2037
01:14:36,585 --> 01:14:38,315
- Hello.
- Hello.

2038
01:14:38,315 --> 01:14:39,885
Do you have a reservation or...

2039
01:14:39,885 --> 01:14:41,015
We have a reservation.

2040
01:14:41,215 --> 01:14:42,655
(Laughing)

2041
01:14:42,655 --> 01:14:44,255
She greets customers at the same time.

2042
01:14:44,355 --> 01:14:45,795
We have an order.

2043
01:14:46,495 --> 01:14:47,725
Three yuzu ades,

2044
01:14:47,725 --> 01:14:49,695
one pomegranate ade, one cake,

2045
01:14:49,695 --> 01:14:52,195
one rice cake pasta, one pizza, one beef burger combo,

2046
01:14:52,195 --> 01:14:54,335
1 tteokbokki for Table 11.

2047
01:14:55,165 --> 01:14:56,765
(Grunting)

2048
01:14:56,765 --> 01:14:58,135
This has to go out, right?

2049
01:14:58,735 --> 01:15:00,875
But I have to make pizza at the same time.

2050
01:15:01,005 --> 01:15:02,145
I'll make the pizza.

2051
01:15:02,145 --> 01:15:04,275
Mimi, we have three orders of pizza.

2052
01:15:04,645 --> 01:15:06,215
- Really?
- We have to make three.

2053
01:15:06,815 --> 01:15:08,245
Yeong Seok, are you very busy?

2054
01:15:08,245 --> 01:15:11,115
- No, I was just...
- Could you please serve these?

2055
01:15:11,115 --> 01:15:12,655
It's an emergency.

2056
01:15:13,655 --> 01:15:15,325
The pollack roe pasta is ready.

2057
01:15:15,325 --> 01:15:17,685
- Yeong Seok, what are you doing?
- One minute, please.

2058
01:15:17,885 --> 01:15:19,325
(Dragging his feet)

2059
01:15:19,325 --> 01:15:21,355
- Middle-aged Man.
- Yes.

2060
01:15:22,595 --> 01:15:23,695
Goodness.

2061
01:15:25,595 --> 01:15:27,365
