2251
01:22:50,745 --> 01:22:52,015
Please wait one moment.

2252
01:22:52,015 --> 01:22:53,015
(When the sous chef cleans the table)

2253
01:22:53,015 --> 01:22:54,075
I'll serve this.

2254
01:22:54,075 --> 01:22:55,115
(The head chef takes the dish that she made.)

2255
01:22:55,115 --> 01:22:56,285
This is insane.

2256
01:22:56,785 --> 01:22:58,555
I made this tteokbokki.

2257
01:22:58,555 --> 01:22:59,815
(We serve the dishes fast.)

2258
01:23:00,085 --> 01:23:02,485
I don't know if I'm serving it right.

2259
01:23:02,485 --> 01:23:03,525
One moment, please.

2260
01:23:03,755 --> 01:23:05,395
- Let me borrow some napkins.
- Okay.

2261
01:23:06,795 --> 01:23:07,795
Thank you.

2262
01:23:08,255 --> 01:23:11,425
(Using the stolen napkins as crocodile mitts)

2263
01:23:11,425 --> 01:23:12,765
Is this right?

2264
01:23:12,895 --> 01:23:14,665
Enjoy your food. Did you order both of them?

2265
01:23:14,665 --> 01:23:15,835
Yes.

2266
01:23:15,835 --> 01:23:17,065
(Anyway, she serves the food safely.)

2267
01:23:17,335 --> 01:23:21,605
(Thanks to the service team, Eun Ji finishes making the ades.)

2268
01:23:22,245 --> 01:23:24,405
(However...)

2269
01:23:24,405 --> 01:23:26,945
Wait, where do these go?

2270
01:23:28,715 --> 01:23:30,145
- You got it, Eun Ji?
- Wait.

2271
01:23:30,145 --> 01:23:31,685
No, nothing is marked.

2272
01:23:31,685 --> 01:23:33,555
You should ask for anyone who didn't get their drink.

2273
01:23:33,555 --> 01:23:34,685
- Should I do that?
- Yes.

2274
01:23:34,685 --> 01:23:36,325
Then I won't mark anything.

2275
01:23:36,325 --> 01:23:37,325
(She decides to use her loud voice.)

2276
01:23:37,325 --> 01:23:38,895
How is the food?

2277
01:23:38,895 --> 01:23:40,125
It's very delicious.

2278
01:23:40,125 --> 01:23:41,495
- Is it good?
- Yes.

2279
01:23:41,495 --> 01:23:42,795
Young Ji, I feel so bad.

2280
01:23:42,795 --> 01:23:44,795
- The drinks are very late.
- It's okay.

2281
01:23:44,795 --> 01:23:45,795
(Eun Ji is carrying an armful of ade.)

2282
01:23:45,795 --> 01:23:48,705
Walk around and check who's still waiting for their pomegranate ade.

2283
01:23:49,105 --> 01:23:50,135
Okay.

2284
01:23:50,135 --> 01:23:51,365
(Young Ji shares the workload to help Eun Ji who's in a rush.)

2285
01:23:51,365 --> 01:23:52,405
Put it here on the tray.

2286
01:23:52,405 --> 01:23:53,675
Okay. Take those three glasses.

2287
01:23:54,535 --> 01:23:57,145
I'm sorry to interrupt, but is anyone waiting for pomegranate ade?

2288
01:23:57,775 --> 01:23:59,075
- I...
- Not pomegranate ade...

2289
01:23:59,075 --> 01:24:00,445
- I'm waiting...
- We're waiting for lemon...

2290
01:24:00,645 --> 01:24:02,485
- I'll go.
- Oh, it's yuzu ade.

2291
01:24:02,685 --> 01:24:04,345
Is anyone waiting for pomegranate ade?

2292
01:24:05,555 --> 01:24:07,115
Is anyone waiting for pomegranate ade?

2293
01:24:07,555 --> 01:24:09,225
- Is anyone waiting for yuzu ade?
- Pomegranate ade...

2294
01:24:09,225 --> 01:24:10,655
- I'm very sorry.
- Thank you.

2295
01:24:10,655 --> 01:24:12,495
Is anyone waiting for pomegranate ade?

2296
01:24:13,525 --> 01:24:15,095
Then why do I have three glasses of pomegranate ade in my hands?

2297
01:24:16,095 --> 01:24:17,565
Did you order two of these?

2298
01:24:17,895 --> 01:24:18,965
- We ordered...
- Well...

2299
01:24:18,965 --> 01:24:20,865
- One yuzu ade and something else.
- One yuzu ade...

2300
01:24:20,865 --> 01:24:21,935
I have your yuzu ade here.

2301
01:24:21,935 --> 01:24:23,235
- One pomegranate ade.
- Yes.

2302
01:24:23,635 --> 01:24:24,765
- Yes. Thank you.
- Thank you.

2303
01:24:25,205 --> 01:24:27,475
Is there anyone who hasn't gotten their pomegranate ade yet?

2304
01:24:27,475 --> 01:24:28,645
Everyone has gotten their ade, right?

2305
01:24:29,675 --> 01:24:30,845
Is this pomegranate ade mine?

2306
01:24:30,845 --> 01:24:33,845
Who hasn't gotten their pomegranate ade yet?

2307
01:24:33,845 --> 01:24:35,145
(She only looks like a pomegranate lover.)

2308
01:24:35,385 --> 01:24:37,285
Give me one glass of pomegranate ade. Thank you.

2309
01:24:37,615 --> 01:24:38,685
You can have that.

2310
01:24:38,685 --> 01:24:40,155
(Smiling)

2311
01:24:40,255 --> 01:24:42,185
- Thank you for your patience.
- Thank you.

2312
01:24:42,185 --> 01:24:43,585
I'm sorry for the wait.

2313
01:24:44,625 --> 01:24:46,325
What does it truly mean to run a business?

2314
01:24:46,625 --> 01:24:48,625
I have absolutely no idea.

2315
01:24:49,465 --> 01:24:51,165
(She serves it right away!)

2316
01:24:51,165 --> 01:24:52,365
- Please enjoy.
- Thank you.

2317
01:24:54,735 --> 01:24:56,465
(Current Time, 2:25pm)

2318
01:24:56,465 --> 01:24:58,505
- Five minutes until last order.
- Okay.

2319
01:24:58,505 --> 01:24:59,635
(5 minutes until last order)

2320
01:25:00,075 --> 01:25:01,605
(The long business hours are finally drawing to a close.)

2321
01:25:01,605 --> 01:25:02,875
Hang in there just a bit longer.

2322
01:25:04,045 --> 01:25:09,145
(The final customers of Space Rice Cake have arrived.)

2323
01:25:09,145 --> 01:25:10,645
I can take your order here.

2324
01:25:11,045 --> 01:25:12,515
May I take your name, please?

2325
01:25:12,515 --> 01:25:13,715
We're just walk-ins...

2326
01:25:13,715 --> 01:25:15,315
- Oh, you're walk-ins. Okay.
- Yes.

2327
01:25:15,725 --> 01:25:17,025
Let's get you seated.

2328
01:25:17,025 --> 01:25:19,025
Before that, we don't have that...

2329
01:25:19,395 --> 01:25:21,395
- Were you in the car earlier?
- Yes, that's us.

2330
01:25:21,395 --> 01:25:22,465
Oh, you made it.

2331
01:25:22,765 --> 01:25:25,225
(The ones that Mimi invited earlier)

2332
01:25:25,835 --> 01:25:29,165
(The customers who were in the car!)

2333
01:25:29,305 --> 01:25:31,705
- Thank you for inviting us.
- Don't mention it.

2334
01:25:32,075 --> 01:25:33,835
One Resurrection Tteokbokki...

2335
01:25:33,835 --> 01:25:36,105
- and one shrimp burger combo, yes?
- Correct.

2336
01:25:36,445 --> 01:25:37,645
- Table Four's order.
- Okay.

2337
01:25:37,645 --> 01:25:39,815
One tteokbokki, one shrimp burger, one yuzu ade,

2338
01:25:39,815 --> 01:25:41,415
- and one Chestnut Tyranno.
- Okay.

2339
01:25:42,045 --> 01:25:43,715
- This is the last order, right?
- Yes.

2340
01:25:44,345 --> 01:25:45,455
- The absolute last order.
- Let's do this.

2341
01:25:45,955 --> 01:25:47,715
- Let's do this.
- Let's really go for it.

2342
01:25:47,715 --> 01:25:48,855
(Putting the pot on the stove to make the last tteokbokki)

2343
01:25:48,855 --> 01:25:51,255
This is the last one. I'll go clean up once I'm done.

2344
01:25:51,255 --> 01:25:53,325
- Okay.
- Young Ji and I will clean up.

2345
01:25:53,325 --> 01:25:54,595
(Into the fryer goes the last shrimp patty.)

2346
01:25:54,695 --> 01:25:56,525
Eun Ji, I'll be done once I wrap this up.

2347
01:25:56,525 --> 01:25:58,865
- I see. Okay.
- I'll join you right away.

2348
01:25:59,735 --> 01:26:03,165
(She stir-fries the ingredients using the skill she mastered.)

2349
01:26:03,505 --> 01:26:06,375
(She carefully adds the final touch, pouring all her heart into it.)

2350
01:26:06,605 --> 01:26:08,335
This is our final moment here. Let's enjoy this moment.

2351
01:26:08,975 --> 01:26:10,505
Let's enjoy this moment.

2352
01:26:10,975 --> 01:26:12,275
This is our last Chestnut Tyranno.

2353
01:26:12,275 --> 01:26:13,615
(Yu Jin, who went through many ups and downs...)

2354
01:26:13,615 --> 01:26:14,845
- Is that the last one?
- Yes.

2355
01:26:16,045 --> 01:26:19,885
(She places the last chestnut.)

2356
01:26:20,355 --> 01:26:22,855
(And there's our service master who did it all.)

2357
01:26:24,185 --> 01:26:27,025
- They're all enjoying the food.
- I'm relieved.

2358
01:26:27,355 --> 01:26:28,455
I'll heat it up.

2359
01:26:29,595 --> 01:26:32,565
(The shrimp burger that got bigger every day)

2360
01:26:32,835 --> 01:26:34,665
Mimi, you fried these so well.

2361
01:26:35,035 --> 01:26:36,735
- It's just incredible.
- Thank you.

2362
01:26:37,005 --> 01:26:38,535
Your emotional support helped me a lot.

2363
01:26:38,535 --> 01:26:39,675
(This is also the end for the tteokbokki.)

2364
01:26:40,605 --> 01:26:42,405
(So they gather the last dishes to be served.)

2365
01:26:42,405 --> 01:26:44,145
The pollack roe and clam pasta is ready.

2366
01:26:44,475 --> 01:26:46,045
I'm all done.

2367
01:26:46,815 --> 01:26:48,445
Here we go, Table Four.

2368
01:26:48,645 --> 01:26:49,745
Thank you.

2369
01:26:50,445 --> 01:26:51,885
- Congratulations.
- We're the last customers.

2370
01:26:51,885 --> 01:26:54,285
You two are the last customers of our restaurant.

2371
01:26:54,655 --> 01:26:55,955
- It must've been hard for you.
- That's not true.

2372
01:26:57,355 --> 01:26:58,655
To be honest, it's been hard.

2373
01:26:59,525 --> 01:27:00,595
I bet you'll love this.

2374
01:27:00,595 --> 01:27:02,055
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2375
01:27:02,395 --> 01:27:03,525
Enjoy your meal.

2376
01:27:04,565 --> 01:27:10,235
(The long business journey is over.)

2377
01:27:10,665 --> 01:27:14,675
(And in the kitchen...)

2378
01:27:15,105 --> 01:27:16,475
Give me a hug.

2379
01:27:17,375 --> 01:27:18,605
Give me a hug.

2380
01:27:18,605 --> 01:27:20,445
(Some of them are sharing a warm hug.)

2381
01:27:20,775 --> 01:27:21,845
Done.

2382
01:27:22,445 --> 01:27:24,445
- Mimi, Young Ji, - We've done a great job.

2383
01:27:24,445 --> 01:27:25,585
- Great job, everyone.
- and Yu Jin.

2384
01:27:25,585 --> 01:27:26,815
- Oh, no. I'm sorry.
- That's okay.

2385
01:27:27,015 --> 01:27:28,015
Honesty,

2386
01:27:28,015 --> 01:27:31,685
- humility, ahk.
- Humility, ahk.

2387
01:27:31,685 --> 01:27:32,795
(Honesty, humility, ahk)

2388
01:27:32,795 --> 01:27:33,895
We've really done a great job.

2389
01:27:33,895 --> 01:27:36,395
Guys, great job. Thank you for your hard work too.

2390
01:27:38,095 --> 01:27:39,935
Look at all those scribbles on her arm.

2391
01:27:40,695 --> 01:27:42,095
- Eun Ji.
- Eun Ji, you look so cool.

2392
01:27:42,805 --> 01:27:45,435
- Eun Ji.
- Once the drink orders backed up,

2393
01:27:45,435 --> 01:27:48,035
- my mind just went blank.
- I know.

2394
01:27:48,335 --> 01:27:49,375
My back hurts.

2395
01:27:49,375 --> 01:27:51,905
(Finally, it's time for the final settlement.)

2396
01:27:51,905 --> 01:27:53,215
We need to tally up the sales...

2397
01:27:53,215 --> 01:27:54,415
What... I wonder what it is.

2398
01:27:54,415 --> 01:27:56,545
I thought we had made enough money to buy five shares of SK Hynix.

2399
01:27:56,545 --> 01:27:58,045
Exactly. How did we end up in the red?

2400
01:27:58,045 --> 01:28:00,215
If you only look at the sales, that makes sense.

2401
01:28:00,485 --> 01:28:03,325
But we had extra expenses.

2402
01:28:03,325 --> 01:28:04,825
- I'll go grab a notebook.
- Hence...

2403
01:28:04,825 --> 01:28:07,195
- The exact amount... We need to...
- Let's figure out what's going on.

2404
01:28:07,455 --> 01:28:09,395
I will document everything. I can't stand this.

2405
01:28:09,595 --> 01:28:11,065
You can take a quick breather first.

2406
01:28:11,065 --> 01:28:12,295
- That's okay. Let's get to it.
- Let's just get right to it.

2407
01:28:12,295 --> 01:28:13,295
- Should we get right to it?
- Just a second.

2408
01:28:13,295 --> 01:28:15,135
- Okay.
- Just in case.

2409
01:28:15,135 --> 01:28:16,705
(She's even bringing the calculator.)

2410
01:28:16,705 --> 01:28:19,075
You said you'd charge us for the accommodation too.

2411
01:28:19,135 --> 01:28:20,635
- I'll give you every detail. Okay.
- That's ridiculous.

2412
01:28:20,775 --> 01:28:21,905
- Then...
- I'm ready to hear you out.

2413
01:28:22,545 --> 01:28:23,805
Let's start with the net sales.

2414
01:28:23,805 --> 01:28:25,045
I'll start with the Goheung branch,

2415
01:28:25,045 --> 01:28:26,875
- the first Earth location.
- Yu Jin, you do the calculation.

2416
01:28:27,245 --> 01:28:29,145
It's 327.80 dollars...

2417
01:28:29,145 --> 01:28:30,245
- for the first day.
- Okay.

2418
01:28:30,245 --> 01:28:31,415
- The 1st day.
- Yes, the 1st day.

2419
01:28:31,815 --> 01:28:33,255
(Sales from the 1st location, Pre-opening day: 93.30 dollars, )

2420
01:28:33,255 --> 01:28:34,615
(Day 1: 327.8 dollars, )

2421
01:28:34,615 --> 01:28:35,985
(Day 2: 832.9 dollars, )

2422
01:28:35,985 --> 01:28:37,385
(Day 3: 809.3 dollars)

2423
01:28:37,385 --> 01:28:38,485
And here are the sales from the Seoul branch.

2424
01:28:38,485 --> 01:28:40,055
(The sales from the 2nd Earth location will be revealed.)

2425
01:28:40,055 --> 01:28:42,665
You sold the food to the staff on the day of cooking practice.

2426
01:28:42,665 --> 01:28:44,395
The sales from that is 210.9 dollars.

2427
01:28:44,765 --> 01:28:46,065
(Sales from the 2nd location, Burger showdown: 210.9 dollars, )

2428
01:28:46,065 --> 01:28:47,265
(Day 1: 1,082.8 dollars, Day 2: 2,050.6 dollars, )

2429
01:28:47,265 --> 01:28:48,495
(Day 3: 2,109.5 dollars, Day 4: 1,075.1 dollars...)

2430
01:28:48,495 --> 01:28:49,705
(including 353.4 dollars from the double event)

2431
01:28:49,835 --> 01:28:52,875
The total sales are 8,945.6 dollars.

2432
01:28:53,905 --> 01:28:56,475
That's almost 10,000 dollars.

2433
01:28:56,475 --> 01:28:57,775
- That's right.
- With just two more zeros,

2434
01:28:57,775 --> 01:28:59,175
- it's 100,000 dollars.
- Now...

2435
01:28:59,175 --> 01:29:00,845
I'd like to congratulate you all, for now.

2436
01:29:00,845 --> 01:29:02,175
- You guys worked so hard.
- Thank you.

2437
01:29:02,175 --> 01:29:03,545
- Thank you.
- Why "for now?"

2438
01:29:03,545 --> 01:29:05,585
We need to hear about the expenses...

2439
01:29:05,585 --> 01:29:08,055
- Let's see the charges.
- I'll break down all the expenses.

2440
01:29:08,285 --> 01:29:10,055
You spent four nights in Goheung, right?

2441
01:29:10,455 --> 01:29:11,785
- That's...
- Wait.

2442
01:29:12,125 --> 01:29:14,025
- The place we stayed at?
- Had we known this,

2443
01:29:14,025 --> 01:29:15,825
- we would've slept on the street.
- Exactly.

2444
01:29:15,825 --> 01:29:17,225
- We would've slept on the bench.
- Right.

2445
01:29:17,225 --> 01:29:18,495
We would've slept on the street.

2446
01:29:18,495 --> 01:29:19,995
- Let's hear her out for now.
- Let me finish first.

2447
01:29:19,995 --> 01:29:22,635
The 4-night stay comes out to 1,200 dollars.

2448
01:29:23,135 --> 01:29:25,305
And you spent another five nights here in Seoul.

2449
01:29:25,405 --> 01:29:26,605
That's 3,800 dollars.

2450
01:29:26,905 --> 01:29:29,305
In Goheung, you drove the car...

2451
01:29:29,305 --> 01:29:30,975
to the grocery store many times.

2452
01:29:31,305 --> 01:29:34,075
The car rental fee is 279.4 dollars.

2453
01:29:34,075 --> 01:29:35,745
Had we known, we would've ridden a bicycle.

2454
01:29:35,745 --> 01:29:37,415
- I would've just walked.
- We would've walked.

2455
01:29:37,415 --> 01:29:39,915
This is basically a multi-level marketing scheme.

2456
01:29:39,915 --> 01:29:41,085
- Exactly.
- A multi-level marketing scheme?

2457
01:29:41,085 --> 01:29:43,355
- I might have to sell heating pads.
- You drove a larger car in Seoul.

2458
01:29:43,355 --> 01:29:45,385
So the car rental fee is 772.25 dollars.

2459
01:29:45,385 --> 01:29:47,395
- We would've just walked.
- Also...

2460
01:29:47,695 --> 01:29:49,595
How did you travel to the second location?

2461
01:29:49,595 --> 01:29:51,195
- You flew here, right?
- What?

2462
01:29:51,365 --> 01:29:53,035
Your flight tickets cost 630.80 dollars.

2463
01:29:53,035 --> 01:29:55,295
We didn't move to Seoul because we wanted to.

2464
01:29:55,295 --> 01:29:56,765
We didn't suggest we should come to Seoul...

2465
01:29:56,765 --> 01:29:58,135
- Wait. We did.
- Yes, we did.

2466
01:29:58,135 --> 01:30:00,135
- Oh, we did.
- I admit it.

2467
01:30:00,135 --> 01:30:02,475
- What else?
- And...

2468
01:30:02,475 --> 01:30:04,175
there's the personnel expenses.

2469
01:30:04,275 --> 01:30:06,715
KARINA worked for about three hours...

2470
01:30:06,715 --> 01:30:08,445
and got paid 30.96 dollars.

2471
01:30:08,445 --> 01:30:10,615
Gabee worked for about five hours...

2472
01:30:10,615 --> 01:30:12,585
and got paid 51.6 dollars.

2473
01:30:12,585 --> 01:30:15,355
Kyung Soo was paid 300 dollars for 12 hours of work.

2474
01:30:15,615 --> 01:30:17,725
- He worked for 12 hours?
- We talked about this, right?

2475
01:30:17,725 --> 01:30:20,225
(Also, the middle-aged man was paid for 64 dollars.)

2476
01:30:20,395 --> 01:30:21,425
- I'm really sorry, - He worked too.

2477
01:30:21,425 --> 01:30:22,865
I feel like I've been slaving away...

2478
01:30:22,865 --> 01:30:25,365
- on a deep-sea fishing boat.
- My point exactly.

2479
01:30:25,595 --> 01:30:27,735
Next up, the rest of the expenses.

2480
01:30:28,195 --> 01:30:30,165
- The mini gimbap was 13.5 dollars.
- Yes.

2481
01:30:30,365 --> 01:30:31,705
That darn mini gimbap.

2482
01:30:31,705 --> 01:30:33,135
I told you not to buy it.

2483
01:30:33,135 --> 01:30:34,505
(Staff meals, groceries, car rental, accommodation, photo printing, )

2484
01:30:34,505 --> 01:30:35,905
(flight fare, personnel expenses, rice cakes provided by the HQ)

2485
01:30:35,905 --> 01:30:38,105
(The total amount: 8,816.75 dollars)

2486
01:30:38,105 --> 01:30:39,475
After deducting all of these...

2487
01:30:40,245 --> 01:30:41,575
After deducting all of these...

2488
01:30:41,975 --> 01:30:43,785
You have 128.85 dollars left.

2489
01:30:44,315 --> 01:30:45,685
- Is that our profit?
- After deducting everything?

2490
01:30:45,685 --> 01:30:47,015
- That's your profit.
- Now...

2491
01:30:47,015 --> 01:30:49,055
- Still, we made a profit.
- Seriously, are you kidding me?

2492
01:30:49,055 --> 01:30:51,385
Now, let's tell them about our injuries.

2493
01:30:51,385 --> 01:30:52,955
- It's our turn now.
- Here we go.

2494
01:30:52,955 --> 01:30:54,795
- First, Eun Ji's fake tattoo.
- First of all,

2495
01:30:54,795 --> 01:30:57,465
- I might get dermatitis.
- Dermatitis.

2496
01:30:57,825 --> 01:30:59,165
I might get dermatitis,

2497
01:30:59,165 --> 01:31:01,035
and I have this inflammatory acne on my left cheek.

2498
01:31:01,035 --> 01:31:02,705
We should also charge them for leg cooling patches.

2499
01:31:02,705 --> 01:31:05,035
- We should.
- They should cover those patches.

2500
01:31:05,335 --> 01:31:07,405
Also, my voice is my livelihood.

2501
01:31:07,635 --> 01:31:09,575
- Me too.
- Because of the ghost pepper...

2502
01:31:09,575 --> 01:31:11,405
- Because of the ghost pepper...
- Pay up for the Little Mermaid tax.

2503
01:31:11,405 --> 01:31:12,445
As for me...

2504
01:31:12,445 --> 01:31:14,345
- I'll show you my hands.
- Right.

2505
01:31:14,515 --> 01:31:16,015
- Oh, gosh. That must be painful.
- She got cuts and bruises.

2506
01:31:16,015 --> 01:31:17,245
I burned my hands too.

2507
01:31:18,285 --> 01:31:19,955
(It's quite an aggressive way of making her point.)

2508
01:31:19,955 --> 01:31:22,155
- I got edema.
- Look at my leg.

2509
01:31:22,155 --> 01:31:24,285
It happened after every shoot.

2510
01:31:24,585 --> 01:31:26,655
- My slim legs got all swollen.
- Raising your legs helps.

2511
01:31:26,795 --> 01:31:28,325
All right. We hear you.

2512
01:31:28,325 --> 01:31:29,825
- My legs...
- I'm just letting you know...

2513
01:31:29,825 --> 01:31:31,225
- how much of a profit you made.
- Gosh, my back hurts.

2514
01:31:31,225 --> 01:31:32,735
- No, that's not right.
- Was it 120 dollars?

2515
01:31:32,735 --> 01:31:34,335
We're saying that we also deserve some reimbursements.

2516
01:31:34,335 --> 01:31:35,765
So? Should we hire an attorney?

2517
01:31:35,765 --> 01:31:37,965
- Let's hire an attorney.
- All right. Then...

2518
01:31:37,965 --> 01:31:40,875
We can start discussing such matters now.

2519
01:31:40,935 --> 01:31:42,575
I just let you know because you were curious...

2520
01:31:42,575 --> 01:31:43,605
- about your net profit.
- And that's 120 dollars?

2521
01:31:43,605 --> 01:31:46,575
- I'd like to make you a deal.
- Okay.

2522
01:31:46,645 --> 01:31:48,115
There are four of us, right?

2523
01:31:48,115 --> 01:31:50,215
And each of us wants a luxury car...

2524
01:31:50,215 --> 01:31:52,145
- like Ferrari, Lamborghini, - Mercedes.

2525
01:31:52,145 --> 01:31:53,685
Mercedes, and Porsche, right?

2526
01:31:54,115 --> 01:31:56,255
How about each of us...

2527
01:31:56,255 --> 01:31:59,125
gets to erase one item?

2528
01:31:59,225 --> 01:32:01,555
- Oh, you mean, from the expenses?
- From the expenses.

2529
01:32:01,555 --> 01:32:03,065
Director Ye Seul, listen to me.

2530
01:32:03,365 --> 01:32:04,765
We worked our tails off.

2531
01:32:04,765 --> 01:32:06,095
The customers are leaving.

2532
01:32:06,095 --> 01:32:08,665
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

2533
01:32:09,435 --> 01:32:11,105
- Just let me tell you one thing.
- Go ahead.

2534
01:32:11,105 --> 01:32:12,605
I'm going to go upstairs...

2535
01:32:12,605 --> 01:32:13,975
to flip all the tables and just lay down.

2536
01:32:13,975 --> 01:32:15,335
I'm going now. Hurry up and follow me.

2537
01:32:15,635 --> 01:32:16,675
(Standing up)

2538
01:32:16,675 --> 01:32:17,775
Come back and sit down for a second.

2539
01:32:18,105 --> 01:32:19,975
- Come on. Sit down for a second.
- We're working with no pay.

2540
01:32:19,975 --> 01:32:20,975
Young Ji.

2541
01:32:20,975 --> 01:32:22,845
We're working without getting paid. Please give us some money.

2542
01:32:22,845 --> 01:32:24,615
I'm coming. Go home safely.

2543
01:32:25,345 --> 01:32:27,185
So, what's your point?

2544
01:32:27,185 --> 01:32:29,925
Are you saying we don't get to erase items from the expenses?

2545
01:32:29,925 --> 01:32:32,825
No. We want to negotiate which items to remove.

2546
01:32:32,825 --> 01:32:35,195
Since when did you negotiate anything with us?

2547
01:32:35,195 --> 01:32:37,265
- I have a question.
- Go ahead.

2548
01:32:37,465 --> 01:32:40,465
Why did you choose such a fancy place in Seoul...

2549
01:32:40,465 --> 01:32:42,605
- like the house from "Parasite?"
- Exactly.

2550
01:32:42,605 --> 01:32:44,435
- You never discussed it with us.
- And you guys stayed upstairs.

2551
01:32:44,435 --> 01:32:45,635
- You just decided on your own.
- You stayed on the second floor.

2552
01:32:45,635 --> 01:32:47,835
- That's right.
- Let's split the cost in half.

2553
01:32:47,835 --> 01:32:48,935
- Then...
- Split the cost in half.

2554
01:32:48,935 --> 01:32:50,605
I agree with you on your stay in Seoul.

2555
01:32:50,605 --> 01:32:52,775
- Will you remove the cost?
- Of course. It should be removed.

2556
01:32:52,775 --> 01:32:55,145
Three staff members stayed there, right?

2557
01:32:55,445 --> 01:32:56,485
- Split the cost?
- Since you're four people,

2558
01:32:56,485 --> 01:32:57,515
we'll split the cost.

2559
01:32:57,515 --> 01:32:59,415
You used both...

2560
01:32:59,415 --> 01:33:01,555
the 2nd and the 3rd floor.

2561
01:33:01,985 --> 01:33:03,855
- Splitting the cost sounds right.
- What?

2562
01:33:03,855 --> 01:33:05,285
- Split the cost.
- Are we splitting the cost?

2563
01:33:05,285 --> 01:33:06,855
- I think...
- Isn't it 4 to 3?

2564
01:33:07,325 --> 01:33:08,595
- Isn't it 4 to 3?
- I don't get...

2565
01:33:08,595 --> 01:33:10,595
why you have to be so aggressive about deducting the expenses?

2566
01:33:10,595 --> 01:33:13,265
Young Ji, we earned 1,900 dollars.

2567
01:33:13,565 --> 01:33:15,335
We made 2,020 dollars.

2568
01:33:15,335 --> 01:33:17,465
- Thank you.
- We should split by 3 to 4.

2569
01:33:17,465 --> 01:33:19,335
Let's do that first.

2570
01:33:19,335 --> 01:33:20,435
- I have a question.
- Yes.

2571
01:33:20,435 --> 01:33:23,075
We never wanted an SUV in Seoul.

2572
01:33:23,075 --> 01:33:25,575
- Exactly. We were fine with Ray.
- We love Ray.

2573
01:33:25,575 --> 01:33:27,375
- Why did you give us an SUV?
- We like Ray.

2574
01:33:27,745 --> 01:33:29,645
As you can hear, the second we got into the SUV,

2575
01:33:29,645 --> 01:33:31,845
Eun Ji said, "We're much better suited..."

2576
01:33:31,845 --> 01:33:33,985
- "to a compact car."
- Really?

2577
01:33:34,185 --> 01:33:36,285
- Because it was cozy.
- We preferred compact cars.

2578
01:33:36,285 --> 01:33:38,425
Let's say that we went overboard...

2579
01:33:38,425 --> 01:33:40,425
- How about...
- with the rental.

2580
01:33:40,425 --> 01:33:41,695
- We'll remove this expense.
- It was so hard for me to drive it.

2581
01:33:41,695 --> 01:33:42,965
- Are you okay with that?
- It was so bulky.

2582
01:33:42,965 --> 01:33:44,895
We'll say that it was 300 dollars...

2583
01:33:44,895 --> 01:33:47,365
and deduct the rest from the earnings.

2584
01:33:47,365 --> 01:33:49,235
- For the Seoul car, 300 dollars.
- Wait.

2585
01:33:49,235 --> 01:33:51,535
- What about the flight?
- I have a question.

2586
01:33:51,535 --> 01:33:53,635
- We could've taken the car.
- We could've taken the car.

2587
01:33:53,635 --> 01:33:55,505
The gas wouldn't have cost that much.

2588
01:33:55,505 --> 01:33:58,505
Did you guys fly so you could bring your equipment?

2589
01:33:58,505 --> 01:34:00,975
- We didn't bring any equipment.
- Then why did we fly?

2590
01:34:00,975 --> 01:34:02,685
We prepared it with your comfort in mind.

2591
01:34:02,685 --> 01:34:04,345
We never asked you to be considerate of us.

2592
01:34:04,945 --> 01:34:06,955
(MOT is overflowing with indignation.)

2593
01:34:07,185 --> 01:34:09,485
- We never asked for it.
- Even if you did...

2594
01:34:10,355 --> 01:34:11,385
(Coughing)

2595
01:34:11,755 --> 01:34:12,855
For the last ten days...

2596
01:34:12,855 --> 01:34:14,025
(The head chef is choking on the harsh reality.)

2597
01:34:14,295 --> 01:34:15,825
We never asked for it.

2598
01:34:16,125 --> 01:34:18,265
Please split the airfare in half.

2599
01:34:18,265 --> 01:34:19,695
- In half?
- Yes, in half.

2600
01:34:20,035 --> 01:34:22,965
- Why did you fly business class?
- Exactly.

2601
01:34:22,965 --> 01:34:24,065
It was only a 30-minute flight.

2602
01:34:24,065 --> 01:34:26,735
Who flies business class from Goheung to Seoul?

2603
01:34:26,735 --> 01:34:27,735
I can't understand.

2604
01:34:27,735 --> 01:34:29,605
We wanted you to travel comfortably. You worked hard.

2605
01:34:29,605 --> 01:34:31,945
Economy or business, it makes no difference.

2606
01:34:31,945 --> 01:34:33,015
That's what I'm saying.

2607
01:34:33,215 --> 01:34:34,675
All right, we'll charge you...

2608
01:34:34,675 --> 01:34:36,145
- only half of the airfare.
- It should be half.

2609
01:34:36,145 --> 01:34:38,585
Let's just call it a day. We'll pay you money.

2610
01:34:39,185 --> 01:34:41,415
Young Ji, we still earned a lot of money.

2611
01:34:41,415 --> 01:34:43,155
How much? Can we buy SK Hynix shares?

2612
01:34:43,355 --> 01:34:46,425
If everything goes well, we could get over 500 dollars each.

2613
01:34:46,425 --> 01:34:47,655
Seriously?

2614
01:34:47,925 --> 01:34:49,095
That's not a small sum.

2615
01:34:49,095 --> 01:34:50,995
Look at this. We earned 1,090 dollars...

2616
01:34:50,995 --> 01:34:52,065
(She's happy yet sad.)

2617
01:34:52,835 --> 01:34:54,565
All right, I'll tell you the result.

2618
01:34:54,695 --> 01:34:57,465
Including the half price and other deductions,

2619
01:34:58,035 --> 01:35:00,605
you made 2,816.5 dollars.

2620
01:35:01,075 --> 01:35:02,435
- Is that our profit?
- That's good.

2621
01:35:02,435 --> 01:35:03,475
That's your total profit.

2622
01:35:03,745 --> 01:35:04,745
(Thankfully, they managed to turn a loss into a profit.)

2623
01:35:04,745 --> 01:35:05,775
Congratulations.

2624
01:35:06,675 --> 01:35:07,675
Thank you.

2625
01:35:08,175 --> 01:35:10,185
- Thank you.
- For letting us make a profit.

2626
01:35:10,185 --> 01:35:12,285
Let's never meet up again.

2627
01:35:13,615 --> 01:35:14,615
(We decide to part ways indefinitely.)

2628
01:35:14,615 --> 01:35:16,485
Let's not see each other for a while.

2629
01:35:16,485 --> 01:35:18,125
- It's been fun.
- Right.

2630
01:35:18,125 --> 01:35:20,455
- With this money, - Do we get 700 dollars?

2631
01:35:20,725 --> 01:35:22,425
- what do you want to do?
- There's something I want.

2632
01:35:22,425 --> 01:35:23,495
- What?
- What?

2633
01:35:23,495 --> 01:35:25,225
I'll take all the ingredients...

2634
01:35:25,225 --> 01:35:28,195
that I used to make tteokbokki, and we'll call it even.

2635
01:35:28,465 --> 01:35:29,465
You can do whatever you want with the rest.

2636
01:35:29,465 --> 01:35:31,465
Young Ji will take equipment we used here...

2637
01:35:31,465 --> 01:35:33,505
- Okay.
- up to her share of the total.

2638
01:35:33,505 --> 01:35:35,475
I want merchandise items...

2639
01:35:35,475 --> 01:35:37,275
- Merchandise?
- worth my share.

2640
01:35:37,375 --> 01:35:39,075
- How about you, Mimi?
- I'd like delivery food.

2641
01:35:39,375 --> 01:35:41,045
- A food delivery gift card...
- A gift card.

2642
01:35:41,045 --> 01:35:42,115
worth your share?

2643
01:35:42,115 --> 01:35:44,645
- Nothing has changed.
- I'll take...

2644
01:35:44,645 --> 01:35:46,515
a voucher for egg is coming services.

2645
01:35:46,715 --> 01:35:48,985
- Worth 700 dollars.
- A 700-dollar voucher?

2646
01:35:49,455 --> 01:35:52,385
Can we give you something that's worth 700 dollars?

2647
01:35:52,385 --> 01:35:54,295
What exactly would that be?

2648
01:35:54,825 --> 01:35:57,595
Let's say that I want to make content for my fans.

2649
01:35:57,925 --> 01:35:59,465
And I want to do it...

2650
01:35:59,465 --> 01:36:00,935
- with egg is coming.
- You want to use our staff?

2651
01:36:00,935 --> 01:36:02,935
- Or I want to go to the HQ.
- That's good.

2652
01:36:02,935 --> 01:36:05,065
Or invite Director Yeong Seok.

2653
01:36:05,065 --> 01:36:06,305
Or invite you, Ye Seul.

2654
01:36:06,305 --> 01:36:07,335
- Yes, that's good.
- That's good.

2655
01:36:07,335 --> 01:36:09,005
- I'm sorry, - But that's...

2656
01:36:09,005 --> 01:36:11,305
but 700 dollars isn't enough to hire me.

2657
01:36:11,305 --> 01:36:12,775
Could you give me a good deal?

2658
01:36:12,775 --> 01:36:15,675
We'll consider what you can get...

2659
01:36:15,675 --> 01:36:17,045
- That's good.
- with 700 dollars.

2660
01:36:17,045 --> 01:36:19,045
All right. Well done, everyone.

2661
01:36:20,415 --> 01:36:22,685
Are we getting released now? Is it over?

2662
01:36:22,685 --> 01:36:23,855
Yes, you're released.

2663
01:36:23,955 --> 01:36:25,755
(Freedom from the place where they dreamed of escaping)

2664
01:36:30,265 --> 01:36:31,895
Honesty.

2665
01:36:31,895 --> 01:36:33,095
Humility.

2666
01:36:33,195 --> 01:36:35,535
- Ahk.
- Ahk.

2667
01:36:35,535 --> 01:36:36,565
Let's hurry.

2668
01:36:37,065 --> 01:36:39,065
- Let's hurry and clean up.
- Well done, everyone.

2669
01:36:39,475 --> 01:36:42,205
- Thank you for your hard work.
- Well done, directors.

2670
01:36:42,575 --> 01:36:43,975
Good job, everyone.

2671
01:36:43,975 --> 01:36:45,605
- Everyone worked so hard.
- This is insane.

2672
01:36:45,605 --> 01:36:46,645
Gosh, my lower back.

2673
01:36:47,975 --> 01:36:49,245
(Back when they were full of confidence...)

2674
01:36:49,245 --> 01:36:50,515
(without knowing what was ahead)

2675
01:36:50,745 --> 01:36:51,945
(The goal of Space Rice Cake)

2676
01:36:52,215 --> 01:36:54,355
(Being cute)

2677
01:36:55,685 --> 01:36:59,185
(What started out as a joke)

2678
01:36:59,525 --> 01:37:00,755
(No one said anything about making rice cakes.)

2679
01:37:00,755 --> 01:37:02,395
(If we actually make rice cakes)

2680
01:37:02,695 --> 01:37:04,065
(I'm being dead serious.)

2681
01:37:04,265 --> 01:37:05,325
(We are...)

2682
01:37:06,235 --> 01:37:07,365
(going to be destroyed.)

2683
01:37:07,895 --> 01:37:11,135
(Then came the ordeal of making rice cakes)

2684
01:37:11,835 --> 01:37:16,245
(Followed by a downpour)

2685
01:37:16,675 --> 01:37:17,705
Hello, village chief.

2686
01:37:17,705 --> 01:37:18,775
(Are you cooking right now?)

2687
01:37:18,905 --> 01:37:20,915
(The village chief appeared like a ray of light.)

2688
01:37:21,375 --> 01:37:23,915
(And the local elders who came by)

2689
01:37:24,515 --> 01:37:26,415
(As the orders kept piling up)

2690
01:37:26,715 --> 01:37:28,185
(An order? No way...)

2691
01:37:29,215 --> 01:37:30,685
(Sometimes, orders got missed.)

2692
01:37:31,285 --> 01:37:33,125
(Empty)

2693
01:37:33,495 --> 01:37:35,095
(Sometimes, they were possessed by wicked spirits.)

2694
01:37:35,625 --> 01:37:39,735
(But the kitchen team fought through it like champs.)

2695
01:37:39,965 --> 01:37:41,695
(Me? I'm an idol singer.)

2696
01:37:42,195 --> 01:37:44,135
(The service team kept smiling brightly.)

2697
01:37:44,605 --> 01:37:47,605
(You don't have to cry)

2698
01:37:48,105 --> 01:37:50,675
(Thanks to Eun Ji's cheekiness)

2699
01:37:51,005 --> 01:37:53,175
(Chestnut Tyranno)

2700
01:37:53,545 --> 01:37:55,415
(Even Yu Jin who was very shy)

2701
01:37:56,185 --> 01:37:59,315
(Zesty pomegranate ade)

2702
01:37:59,585 --> 01:38:01,815
(She came out of her shell.)

2703
01:38:02,685 --> 01:38:04,825
(I'm not skilled enough to make 2.)

2704
01:38:05,085 --> 01:38:07,155
(Mimi who used to struggle with one order of rice cake pasta)

2705
01:38:09,225 --> 01:38:11,765
(She was handling group orders at once.)

2706
01:38:12,095 --> 01:38:14,695
(Young Ji who was always trembling with anxiety)

2707
01:38:15,165 --> 01:38:18,935
(Thanks to the others' endless encouragement)

2708
01:38:19,135 --> 01:38:20,175
(Who am I? I'm Lee Young Ji.)

2709
01:38:20,505 --> 01:38:22,635
(She became so much more composed.)

2710
01:38:23,145 --> 01:38:25,245
(But one thing never changed.)

2711
01:38:25,545 --> 01:38:26,745
(Gasping)

2712
01:38:27,045 --> 01:38:28,175
(Gasping)

2713
01:38:28,415 --> 01:38:30,115
(Mimi, look at this.)

2714
01:38:30,345 --> 01:38:32,085
(Taking pictures of empty plates)

2715
01:38:32,485 --> 01:38:34,355
(Taking pictures again and again)

2716
01:38:34,815 --> 01:38:39,455
(The sense of pride they felt every time they saw an empty plate)

2717
01:38:40,025 --> 01:38:42,455
(Even when they were exhausted and worn out)

2718
01:38:42,965 --> 01:38:47,365
(They always found ways to lift each other up.)

2719
01:38:47,795 --> 01:38:49,865
(And)

2720
01:38:50,265 --> 01:38:52,535
(Manager of new menu development from the HQ)

2721
01:38:53,135 --> 01:38:58,805
(Everyone who rushed over to lend us a helping hand)

2722
01:38:59,915 --> 01:39:02,245
(And Yang Hee Eun)

2723
01:39:02,645 --> 01:39:07,685
(We thank every person who was part of this journey.)

2724
01:39:08,215 --> 01:39:11,655
(Their first day of business in Goheung on a rainy day)

2725
01:39:12,125 --> 01:39:14,955
(To their final day of business in Seoul on a rainy day)

2726
01:39:16,295 --> 01:39:18,695
(It's time to bring the curtain down.)

2727
01:39:18,695 --> 01:39:20,695
Thank you for your hard work.

2728
01:39:21,695 --> 01:39:22,905
Well done.

2729
01:39:22,905 --> 01:39:23,965
(Epilogue)

2730
01:39:24,465 --> 01:39:26,205
I'm about to cry now.

2731
01:39:28,175 --> 01:39:29,605
Isn't it hard to leave?

2732
01:39:29,605 --> 01:39:31,775
- Now that we have to leave...
- It's so sad.

2733
01:39:31,775 --> 01:39:33,115
It's making me cry.

2734
01:39:33,115 --> 01:39:34,775
Aren't you sad to leave the kitchen?

2735
01:39:34,775 --> 01:39:37,015
I can't leave.

2736
01:39:37,515 --> 01:39:39,445
It's sad to leave the kitchen.

2737
01:39:39,655 --> 01:39:42,955
It's really making me cry.

2738
01:39:43,225 --> 01:39:44,655
Can I change my voucher?

2739
01:39:45,325 --> 01:39:46,325
- Now?
- Yes.

2740
01:39:46,325 --> 01:39:48,725
A voucher that lets me work at Space Rice Cake when I want.

2741
01:39:48,725 --> 01:39:50,495
- No way.
- A voucher.

2742
01:39:52,325 --> 01:39:55,065
- No way.
- We might want to do it someday.

2743
01:39:55,635 --> 01:39:57,065
That sounds good. Do you want to change it?

2744
01:39:57,335 --> 01:39:59,065
- Do you want to change it?
- Do you want to change it?

2745
01:39:59,065 --> 01:40:01,475
- The others should know too.
- Right.

2746
01:40:03,345 --> 01:40:04,605
Eun Ji.

2747
01:40:05,605 --> 01:40:07,275
- Yu Jin.
- Yes?

2748
01:40:07,745 --> 01:40:10,245
- Yu Jin.
- How about a voucher...

2749
01:40:10,245 --> 01:40:12,485
- that lets us work...
- My tears completely stopped.

2750
01:40:12,485 --> 01:40:15,515
at Space Rice Cake whenever we want?

2751
01:40:15,515 --> 01:40:16,585
How about changing it to that?

2752
01:40:20,455 --> 01:40:23,025
We can't do it unless we ask for it.

2753
01:40:23,725 --> 01:40:24,765
Right.

2754
01:40:24,765 --> 01:40:26,765
- Hold on.
- Don't you like the idea?

2755
01:40:28,295 --> 01:40:30,965
- Eun Ji.
- She's talking about a voucher.

2756
01:40:31,205 --> 01:40:33,505
Working at Space Rice Cake when we want.

2757
01:40:33,605 --> 01:40:34,605
You want to do this again?

2758
01:40:38,005 --> 01:40:39,505
- You want to do it again?
- I mean,

2759
01:40:39,505 --> 01:40:42,575
we can't do it unless we say that we want to.

2760
01:40:42,575 --> 01:40:45,045
- All four of us have to agree.
- Exactly.

2761
01:40:45,045 --> 01:40:47,485
- I like that.
- We can do it when we want.

2762
01:40:47,485 --> 01:40:48,915
That's a great idea.

2763
01:40:49,015 --> 01:40:50,025
- It works...
- I like it.

2764
01:40:50,025 --> 01:40:52,685
if we never say that we want to do it.

2765
01:40:53,795 --> 01:40:55,495
- We should do it, Eun Ji.
- Of course.

2766
01:40:55,495 --> 01:40:57,225
- We should do it with gratitude.
- We should.

2767
01:40:57,225 --> 01:40:58,695
- Everyone.
- Yes?

2768
01:40:58,695 --> 01:41:00,395
We'll bid each other farewell.

2769
01:41:01,095 --> 01:41:02,865
Let's not see each other for a while.

2770
01:41:03,265 --> 01:41:05,565
Thank you for putting up...

2771
01:41:05,565 --> 01:41:08,075
with each other's wicked spirit, especially mine.

2772
01:41:08,075 --> 01:41:09,075
- Thank you.
- Honesty.

2773
01:41:09,075 --> 01:41:10,575
- Humility.
- Humility.

2774
01:41:10,575 --> 01:41:12,145
- Ahk.
- Ahk.

2775
01:41:12,145 --> 01:41:13,815
Clocking out. Forever.

2776
01:41:15,245 --> 01:41:17,015
(The end)

2777
